outh, with the burial chamber under the wider northern end [1]. Today the cairn has been badly robbed and the main features are the five large gritstone slabs, the remains of the burial chamber [1]. Pikestones is the earliest man-made structure in the area and only one other chambered tomb has been found in Lancashire [1]. The monument must have taken an immense amount of labour to construct and like most long barrows was erected in a prominent position, located on a ridge at a height of just over 900 feet [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92413", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92414", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:141972", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-001: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8d/Pikestones_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1892027.jpg'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245565", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245566", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331328", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/01ef71b0/Pikestones - geograph.org.uk - 1892027.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384930", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384931", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
