raulic engineering within Toletum, which during the Imperial era featured large public works including bath buildings and two aqueducts.'' -> ''Located beneath Calle Nuncio Viejo, these Roman vaults consist of a system of walls and barrel vaults dating to the Roman era according to archaeological studies [1] [2]. They sit near two of the city\\''s most important Roman remains: the Roman baths and cisterns of the water distribution network [3] [4]. Restored and enhanced by the Toledo Consortium by April 2008, they are now accessible to visitors through the \"Unknown Heritage\" (Patrimonio Desconocido) guided routes programme [1] [5] [6].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245575", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245576", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346236", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346237", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
