has continued at the site, funded by English Heritage, the BBC, the British Museum and the Kent Archaeological Society [1]. This work has indicated that the now ploughed-away barrow was as high as 5m and had a diameter of more than 40m [1]. The flat-bottomed ditch that surrounded it was 5–6 m wide and 1.35 m deep [1]. Considerable evidence of much earlier Neolithic activity has now been found on the site including by far the largest assemblage of grooved ware in the county [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142637", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8c/Claw_beaker_from_Ringmere_Farm_BM_2005.12-5.1.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/08122cd2/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('082935cc-6367-40a7-86e5-dd01e0be5b1c'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:082935cc-6367-40a7-86e5-dd01e0be5b1c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''4'' restored on Hampton Down Stone Circle', '087e9a289145dadb71ceba3fbef3810c', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Stone circle'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 37 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81700", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2040:chunk-0001: description ''The Hampton Down Stone Circle is a prehistoric monument near Portesham in Dorset, England. Archaeologists believe it was erected during the Late Neolithic to Early Bronze Age period (3300–900 BCE), part of a broad tradition of stone circle construction across Britain, Ireland, and Brittany. The original purpose remains unknown, though it likely served as a religious or ceremonial site. Some scholars suggest the stones may not form a true circle but are instead kerbstones from a Bronze Age round barrow.'' -> ''Positioned at the national grid reference 35960865, Hampton Down Stone Circle is located on the southern edge of an open downland ridge at a height of 680 feet above sea level [1]. A photograph from 1908 showed sixteen stones as part of the monument [1]. However, by 1964 twenty-eight stones were found to be part of the circle [1]. In 1964 the stones in the circle were disturbed by agricultural activity [1]. It was then decided that the site would be excavated, a project which was ordered by the Ministry of Public Building and Works and carried out in May 1965 under the directorship of Geoffrey J. Wainwright [1]. The excavation revealed that the location of the stones was not their original prehistoric position [1]. The original location of the circle was identified as existing a few feet to the west [1]. The original circle had either eight or possibly nine sockets for stones and was oval shaped [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92522", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:92523", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245631", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245632", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333623", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/082935cc/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/082935cc/Hampton Down stone circle - geograph.org.uk - 242207.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346272", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346273", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2050''"}]'::jsonb),
