 objects that date to approximately 120,000-130,000 years ago, during the Paleolithic period [1]. If authentically dated, these artifacts would represent the only known Neanderthal presence in the Nordic countries [1].'' -> ''Wolf Cave (Finnish: Susiluola) is a natural cave formation at the border of Kristinestad and Karijoki municipalities in Finland [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246061", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246062", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346320", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346321", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
