    ('1268a0fc-ad34-46f1-878c-4cb4402d9cfa'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '1', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:1268a0fc-ad34-46f1-878c-4cb4402d9cfa:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''1'' restored on Moel y Gaer, Rhosesmor', '3375973e0c68aa5af1a2174bbeb8fdf0', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 86 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81934", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2047:chunk-0001: description ''Moel y Gaer is an Iron Age hillfort situated on a summit at the southern end of Halkyn Mountain overlooking the Dee Estuary near Rhosesmor, Flintshire, Wales[1]. Excavations in the early 1970s uncovered a complex sequence of timber defensive structures and multiple phases of building work within the ramparts[1]. The site is exceptionally well-preserved, with its earthworks remaining visible across the hilltop[1].'' -> ''Moel y Gaer is an Iron Age hillfort located on a summit at the southern end of Halkyn Mountain, overlooking the village of Rhosesmor, Flintshire [1]. It is a well-preserved hillfort overlooking the Dee Estuary [1]. Excavations in the early 1970s revealed a sequence of defensive structures made of timber and several phases of building work inside the ramparts [1]. Excavations suggest that the site was occupied, perhaps sporadically, from the Neolithic period to sometime before the Roman conquest of the area [1]. Remains of a timber long house on the hill summit have been dated to the third millennium BC and may represent the 