n Empire [1]. It is composed of a single arch and parapet, and has undergone several changes over the centuries [1]. On its south side is a section of a Roman path, about 50 meters long, which gives access to the bridge [1]. Close to the bridge archaeologists have identified vestiges of a Roman-era cemetery together with remains of a Neolithic settlement [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93440", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93441", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143430", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-003: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/Catribana1.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/15cf53da/Catribana1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246113", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246114", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384986", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
