he fragmentary remains of two adults and a child along with pottery shards from the Neolithic era [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94358", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94359", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143518", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/186eeb54/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/186eeb54/Neolithic Chamber Tomb at Broadsands - geograph.org.uk - 2061514.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235484", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235485", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331456", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/186eeb54/Neolithic Chamber Tomb at Broadsands - geograph.org.uk - 2061514.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/186eeb54/Neolithic Chamber Tomb at Broadsands - geograph.org.uk - 2061841.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1876d7d8-2561-4f0b-8278-f89293aecbb7'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:1876d7d8-2561-4f0b-8278-f89293aecbb7:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Lee Wood', '276d07cbeb3e089a9e8bc9b48fbb36a9', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(51.11991445684041, -4.164732189309845, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33179", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0016:chunk-0001: description ''Lee Wood is an Iron Age hillslope enclosure near Braunton and Barnstaple in Devon, situated on a promontory above Knowle Water at approximately 120 metres above sea level. The fort is about 70 paces in diameter on the western spur of a hill overlooking the valley. Discovered in the late 1950s by a local farmer, the woodland covering the earthwork was cleared in the 1960s-70s, partially uncovering a fireplace containing ashes and animal bone including pig from the Neolithic period. Extensive Mesolithic and Neolithic artifacts found nearby include flint scrapers, serrated blades, burins, knives, and arrowheads verified by the University of Exeter.'' -> ''Lee Wood is the location of an Iron Age enclosure or hill fort situated near to Braunton and Barnstaple in Devon [1]. The enclosure is situated on a sloping hillside forming a promontory above the Knowle Water at approx 120 metres above sea level to the northeast of Braunton and northwest of Barnstaple [1]. The woods that once covered this earthwork were cut down in the 1960s and during this work a fireplace was partially uncovered [1]. The exposed portion of the fireplace contained ashes and small pieces of animal bone, including pig, dating from the Neolithic period [1]. The fort is about 70 paces in diameter, and is located on the western spur of a hill overlooking to the west the valley of Knowle Water [1]. Many Mesolithic and Neolithic flint scrapers, serrated blades, backed blades, burins, knives, and arrowheads as well as slingshots and other stones showing signs of having been used as tools have been found near the fort [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94360", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94361", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94362", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235486", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: site_type None -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246459", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246460", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384994", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384995", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
