ast seven stone circles that are known to have been erected in the area south of Swindon in northern Wiltshire [1]. Around the 1860s, the megaliths of Fir Clump stone circle were levelled [1]. Some of the fallen megaliths were rediscovered in 1965 by the archaeologist Richard Reiss, who described and measured the monument [1]. In 1969, these stones were removed during construction of the M4 motorway [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94408", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94409", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246485", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246486", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347145", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347146", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
