nternal area [1]. The main enclosure has a single rampart and ditch, with steep drops on the north, east and south sides [1]. The bank is up to 1.6 metres high with a ditch 2 metres deep [1]. There is an additional rampart 30 metres to the west, with a deep ditch [1]. The rampart is revetted with drystone walling [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143989", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1b8b5fd4/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1b8b5fd4/Bury Castle.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:307758", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1b8b5fd4/Bury Castle.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1b8b5fd4/Geograph 3319707 Site of Bury Castle, Iron Age Fort.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
