s of its architectural features[1].\" -> ''Al-Mnaykhrat or Mnechret is a late sixth-century BC Greek rock-tomb near Marj, in northeastern Libya [1]. The tomb is cut into a cliff on the west side of the Wadi Taybsillu, southeast of the city of Marj [1]. It is clearly visible across the surrounding plain and must have been built for a high-ranking individual, but there is no evidence regarding their identity [1]. The structure is dated to the late sixth century BC on stylistic grounds [1]. The tomb is about 2.15 metres above the ground level [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94446", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94447", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94448", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: site_type ''Tomb'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235544", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235545", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-600''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235546", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: site_type None -> ''Tomb''"}]'::jsonb),
