for gate-posts [1]. In 1925 a Doctor Quine of Frizington \"restored\" the stone circle, setting the stones in concrete [1]. Whether or not he erected the stones in their original stone holes is unclear, and it is unlikely that all of the re-erected stones come from the original circle [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94460", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94461", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246511", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246512", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347163", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347164", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
