]. The irregular trapezoid-shaped fortress was built of cut stone and brick with lime mortar bonding [1]. Walls are preserved up to 4 metres in places, with towers at the east, south, and west ends, and a gate flanked by two towers on the north wall [1] [5]. The remains follow the terrain configuration [1]. Designated a cultural heritage site on 1 March 1986, under the protection of the Republic of Serbia [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235567", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: site_type None -> ''Fortification''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246519", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246520", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345663", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345664", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
