mic views across the Cotswolds to the River Severn under clear conditions [1][3]. Since 1971, Swindon Borough Council has managed the 42-hectare site as a country park, preserving its archaeological and landscape value [1][3].'' -> ''Barbury Castle is an Iron Age hillfort in Wiltshire, England [1] [2]. Located about 5.5 miles south of Swindon on Barbury Hill, it sits along the ancient Ridgeway route—a prehistoric pathway crossing the chalk downs of southern England [1] [3]. The fortification features two deep defensive ditches and ramparts [1]. The site lies within the Wessex Downs Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty and commands views across the Cotswolds to the River Severn under clear conditions [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235611", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235612", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-700''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308510", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/230e6523/Barbury Castle Aerial View (2).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/230e6523/Barbury_Hill_Iron_Age_Fort.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('235def6a-3971-4308-9248-172c2cb39025'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:235def6a-3971-4308-9248-172c2cb39025:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''6'' restored on Day House Lane Stone Circle', '1e69e5ce0f09a27421208879d34b4473', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Stone circle'', ''Undated'') is shared by 40 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33427", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0018:chunk-0001: description ''Day House Lane Stone Circle, also known as Coate Stone Circle, is a Late Neolithic to Early Bronze Age sarsen megalith circle near Coate on the southeastern edge of Swindon, Wiltshire. Antiquarian A. D. Passmore estimated the original diameter at approximately 69 metres with over thirty stones; by the 1890s only nine survived, reduced to five partly buried stones by the early 21st century. It was one of at least seven stone circles erected in the area south of Swindon, part of a wider ritual landscape linked to nearby Avebury (9 miles southwest). The site is a Scheduled Monument protected under the Ancient Monuments and Archaeological Areas Act 1979.'' -> \"Day House Lane Stone Circle, also known as Coate Stone Circle, is a stone circle near the hamlet of Coate, now on the southeastern edge of Swindon, in the English county of Wiltshire [1]. Five partly buried stones remain at the site [1]. A circle of sarsen megaliths, Day House Lane Stone Circle probably had an original diameter of about 69 metres and possibly contained over thirty stones [1]. It was one of at least seven stone circles that are known to have been erected in the area south of Swindon in northern Wiltshire [1]. The earliest known reference to the site was made by the local writer Richard Jefferies in the 1860s [1]. When the antiquarian A. D. Passmore investigated the site during the 1890s he found nine stones, mostly buried [1]. He observed a line of five stones not far from the circle''s northern end, suggesting that these were part of a prehistoric avenue connected to the circle; these too no longer existed by the 21st century [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95248", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246883", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246884", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347190", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347191", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
