oving on to Maiden Castle [1]. There is no evidence that the Romans settled at Abbotsbury Castle as they did at some other hill forts [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95255", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95256", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144683", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/23cb48d4/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/23cb48d4/Abbotsbury Castle interior.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246887", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246888", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308518", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/23cb48d4/Abbotsbury Castle interior.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/23cb48d4/Dorset_abbotsbury_castle_earthworks.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385035", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385036", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('23ddb957-c31f-4ec9-9fcc-e02bc5316c5c'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:23ddb957-c31f-4ec9-9fcc-e02bc5316c5c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''8'' restored on Rockbourne Roman Villa', '8015544197b0d6f930c344fee1ef75e7', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Residence/villa/farmhouse'', ''Undated'') is shared by 6 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33443", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0019:chunk-0001: description ''Rockbourne Roman Villa is a Roman courtyard villa in Hampshire, England [1]. Discovered in 1942 by a local farmer, it was excavated over three decades by A. T. Morley Hewitt [1]. Today the villa is open to the public.'' -> ''Rockbourne Roman villa is located at West Park, near the village of Rockbourne in Hampshire [1]. The villa was discovered in 1942 by a farmer digging out a ferret [1]. Originally the site was occupied by a timber roundhouse with a chalk floor, of a type common in the Late Iron Age [1]. In the 1st century this was replaced by a small rectangular stone house [1]. In 1967 a hoard of 7717 bronze coins was found buried in a pottery jar on the site [1]. By the 4th century the villa was now a large courtyard villa enclosed on at least three sides [1]. In total there were probably around 40 rooms in use [1]. Of particular interest are two much-damaged Roman milestones found re-used in the building fabric of the villa [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95259", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fi