 by Lt Col William Hawley, and in 2003–2004 by English Heritage [1]. Permission was granted for full excavation in 2012–2014 in order to record the site, which was being extensively damaged by badgers [1]. Many Bronze Age items were found, with a smaller quantity from the Neolithic period [1]. Many Saxon graves were uncovered, together with items including a bucket-shaped drinking vessel, made from pieces of yew wood bound together with bronze [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95263", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95264", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235617", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235618", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('241df2d5-69c9-47e0-9df3-105a26a4d141'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:241df2d5-69c9-47e0-9df3-105a26a4d141:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Carl Wark', '069fc1280b431f6f0136bc64e1505347', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(53.32955970533958, -1.612734887324762, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82312", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2058:chunk-0001: description \"Carl Wark is an Iron Age hillfort on Hathersage Moor in the Peak District, just inside Sheffield''s boundary in South Yorkshire[1]. The rocky promontory is defended by vertical cliffs on three sides, with a prehistoric embankment protecting the fourth side[1]. The date of construction and purpose of the fortifications remain unknown, though it is typically assigned to the Iron Age period[1]. The site is a scheduled monument and lies near Higger Tor[1][2].\" -> \"Carl Wark (sometimes Carl''s Wark) is a rocky promontory on Hathersage Moor in the Peak District National Park, just inside the boundary of Sheffield, England [1]. The promontory is faced by vertical cliffs on all but one side, which is protected by a prehistoric embankment [1]. The cliffs and embankment form an enclosure that has been interpreted as an Iron Age hill fort, though the date of construction and purpose of the fortifications remains unknown [1]. Carl Wark is located at grid reference SK259814, at an elevation of about 370 metres above sea level [1]. The promontory is approximately 230 metres long and 60 metres wide, oriented south-east to north-west [1]. The southern edge of the enclosure consists of large earth-fast boulders that have been reinforced with millstone grit blocks, forming a wall 2–2.5 metres high [1]. A rampart across the western end of the promontory completes the enclosure [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114847", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114848", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114849", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144689", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/241df2d5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/241df2d5/Carl Wark Fort.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246895", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246896", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308530", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/241df2d5/Carl Wark Fort.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/241df2d5/Carl_Wark_rampart_face_20090912.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385037", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385038", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
