eum, Middlesbrough, in 1927, uncovered parts of an earthenware cremation urn, together with burnt bone and flint [1]. These possibly dated from 1800 BC [1]. There was a substantial Iron Age hill fort at Eston Nab [1]. Boulder walls and ditches are still visible even though they were built in around 700 BC [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114859", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114860", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-6000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114861", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: site_type ''Mound/tumulus'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145350", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/277970ce/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/277970ce/Eston Nab from Flatts Lane.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235639", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235640", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-700''"}]'::jsonb),
