haeological site in the Lake Titicaca basin to be systematically excavated [1]. Archaeologists have identified 36 cultural strata at the site [1]. From 7500 to 4000 BP, Qillqatani was inhabited by hunter-gatherers as a seasonal campsite [1]. These early occupants hunted mostly camelids, and some deer [1]. From 3660 BP onwards, Qillqatani was inhabited by pastoralist camelid-herders who built houses and began to occupy the site long-term [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35703", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: site_type ''Archaeological site'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95385", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95386", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-5500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95387", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Rock art''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235669", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235670", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-7000''"}]'::jsonb),
