iameter along with slingstones, hammer-stones, clay daub, and part of a stone mace. The site is crossed by the Wales Coast Path.'' -> ''An Iron Age promontory hillfort perched on 60-metre cliffs on the Gower coast near Rhossili, Swansea, Wales [1] [2] [3]. Ceramic evidence dates occupation to circa 50 BC - 50 AD, with pottery of Glastonbury type found on site [2] [3]. Excavations in 1938 uncovered slingstones, hammer-stones, clay daub, and part of a stone mace [2] [3]. The site is crossed by the Wales Coast Path [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235676", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235677", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-200''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:339374", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-002-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/2a453751/The Knave - geograph.org.uk - 7016403.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347252", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347253", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-200'' -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
