 Most are south of the A35 road, with a few north of the road [1]. They date from about 1500 BC [1]. The barrows, individually or in groups, are separately listed as ancient monuments [1]. There is a minor plateau on the west of the site, from which all the barrows can be seen [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114907", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145507", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9f/Barrows_near_Kingston_Russell._-_geograph.org.uk_-_1075574.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2b2d0e62/Winterbourne Poor Lot Barrows II.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
