economic context behind megalithic site placement in prehistoric Corsica.'' -> ''Pughjaredda (also spelled Poghjaredda) is a megalithic archaeological site in the commune of Sotta, southern Corsica, dating to the Middle Neolithic period (ca. 5000-4000 BC) [1] [2] [3] [4]. The site features dolmens, menhirs, and stone circles, along with evidence of domestic dwelling and funerary activities [2]. Studies at Pughjaredda have provided key insights into Corsican-Sardinian megalithism [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235687", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: lat ''41.5457001069429'' -> ''41.570833''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235688", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: lon ''9.195523410159458'' -> ''9.199167''"}]'::jsonb),
