1]. A Paleolithic hand axe was found here [1]. To the south-west of the fort are the remains of a lynchet, consisting of a steep 2-metre high scarp that runs parallel to the fort''s defences [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96303", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96304", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246975", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246976", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308692", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2bfc5712/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2bfc5712/Southwest ditch and rampart at Clearbury Ring - geograph.org.uk - 177614.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385060", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385061", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
