rce": "remediation_change_log:347288", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385071", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385072", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-2500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('2f217cc8-9aad-4f87-93fb-c8732fe85e39'::uuid, 'mystery', '2', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:2f217cc8-9aad-4f87-93fb-c8732fe85e39:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''6'' restored on Portus Lemanis', 'cfabc598d21fff1792b13be25517dfd1', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 2 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''Undated'') is shared by 187 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82624", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2066:chunk-0001: description ''Portus Lemanis (Latin for \"Port of the Leman\"), also recorded as Lemanae, was a Roman Saxon Shore fort, settlement and port in southern Kent, England. The fortification, dating to the 3rd century AD, occupied a strategic hilltop position overlooking what was then a sea inlet—now the drained Romney Marsh. The site, known locally as Stutfall Castle, sits on private land accessible by public footpath. The modern village of Lympne derives its name directly from this ancient port.'' -> ''Portus Lemanis, also known as Lemanae, was the Latin name of a Roman Saxon Shore fort, settlement and port in southern Kent [1]. The first documentary mention of the site is found in the late 3rd-century Antonine Itinerary [1]. According to the 5th-century Notitia Dignitatum, the fort was garrisoned by a regiment raised in Tournai and formed part of a defence system known as the Saxon Shore under the command of a Count [1]. The last mention of Lemanis in Latin sources is in the late 7th-century Ravenna Cosmography, by which time the site, along with the rest of Britain, had long been severed from the Roman Empire [1]. The fort stood on a hill overlooking a reach of sea which has since been drained to form the Romney Marsh [1]. The construction of the Saxon Shore-era fort can be dated to the late 270s, as is evidenced by its late-style characteristics [1]. The southern side of the fort is wholly missing, and elsewhere the remains have been moved at various angles, while little evidence of interior structures (remains of a bath and possibly the principia) survives [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96373", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96374", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146241", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c2/Archaeological_excavations_of_the_East_Gate_of_Portus_Lemanis_in_1976_-_retouched.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2f217cc8/Lemanis Osttor FM.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247349", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247350", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309354", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2f217cc8/Lemanis Osttor FM.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2f217cc8/Archaeological_excavations_of_the_East_Gate_of_Portus_Lemanis_in_1976_-_retouched.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345665", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345666", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quo