 bases and there is only one archway [1]. The entablature rests on four Corinthian columns placed at the extremities of each corner, such that a quarter of each drum is embedded in the monument [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146296", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3199f739/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3199f739/Arco_di_Augusto-Susa.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('31efd673-3b29-4dbc-acb2-2d9179d7a972'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:31efd673-3b29-4dbc-acb2-2d9179d7a972:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: antiquity ''7'' restored on The Bull Ring', 'b0b80a7eaf2f72517a0f81731b03b00e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33579", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0022:chunk-0001: description ''The Bull Ring is a Class II henge monument near Dove Holes in Derbyshire, England, dating to the Late Neolithic to Early Bronze Age period (c. 3000-1500 BC). The monument measures approximately 93m by 90m externally, with a rock-cut ditch (8-12m wide) and surrounding bank, enclosing an oval interior of 53m by 46m with north and south entrances. Local tradition records that large stones forming a circle within the henge were removed for building material over a century ago. Excavations in 1902 and 1949 yielded flint tools, Beaker pottery, antler tines, and ox bones. Two barrows (one oval, one bowl) stand about 20m away.'' -> ''The Bull Ring is a Class II henge that was built in the Late Neolithic period near Dove Holes in Derbyshire, England [1]. The henge consists of a large, circular earthwork, which is currently about 1 metre high and 9–11 metres wide; however it was originally 2 metres high and 5.5–7 metres wide [1]. The henge has a ditch on the inside, which varies between 0.5 and 1 metre deep and 8 and 12 metres wide; it was originally 1.2–2 metres deep and 5–6.5 metres wide [1]. The ditch and bank are separated by a berm, which was originally 5 metres wide [1]. It encloses an area 53 by 46 metres, with entrances to the north and south, each of which have a causeway across the ditch [1]. A minor excavation was carried out in the west ditch in 1902 by Micah Salt; this reputedly discovered some pottery sherds and flint flakes, which have since been lost [1]. A trial excavation by Oxford University Archaeological Society in 1949 established that the ring has two entrances, and also provided information about the original size of the bank and ditch [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96444", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96445", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/75/BullRingDoveHoles.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/31efd673/The Bull Ring Henge 3.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247383", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247384", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309394", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/31efd673/The Bull Ring Henge 3.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/31efd673/BullRingDoveHoles.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385081", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385082", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period