t, and Anglo-Saxon renovation of the defenses. A D-shaped Middle Iron Age hut was discovered during 1960 excavations. The site has been a Scheduled Monument since 1925.\" -> ''Whitsbury Castle Ditches is an Iron Age hillfort near Whitsbury in Hampshire, on a chalk outcrop [1]. Excavations reveal multi-period use spanning from Mesolithic activity through Bronze Age ranch boundaries, Iron Age settlement, and Anglo-Saxon renovation of the defenses [1]. A D-shaped Middle Iron Age hut was discovered during 1960 excavations [2]. The site has been a Scheduled Monument since 1925 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236568", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236569", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-600''"}]'::jsonb),
