]. In Barrow J he found an intact main burial chamber containing a crushed red collared urn, decorated with cord impressions, inverted over burned bone [1]. He also found numerous secondary cremations and stone tools, leading him to classify the builders as the \"Yorkshire Food Vessel Culture\" in the terminology of the time [1]. The site also contained evidence of later Romano-British occupation [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97149", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97150", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247405", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247406", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347320", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347321", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385095", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385096", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-2000'' -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
