 area derives its name Panchavati, and sits near the revered Kalaram Temple.'' -> ''Sita Gufa is a sacred cave in Panchavati, Nashik, Maharashtra, deeply connected to the Hindu epic Ramayana [1] [2] [3]. According to tradition, this is where Goddess Sita lived with Lord Rama during their 14-year exile and where she was abducted by the demon king Ravana [1] [2] [4].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247421", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247422", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345669", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345670", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
