a Scheduled Ancient Monument [1]. Lamyatt Beacon, the highest point of the hill, hosts the remains of a Romano-Celtic temple built in the late 3rd century AD, in use until the early 5th century [1] [2]. A burial ground with 16 graves lies north of the temple, and a sunken chamber to the south showed marks of burning [2] [3] [4].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236617", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: lat ''51.118409868462685'' -> ''51.1282''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236618", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: lon ''-2.47207381629472'' -> ''-2.47845''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247433", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247434", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385101", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385102", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
