rn end near Milton Clevedon, designated a Scheduled Ancient Monument [1]. Lamyatt Beacon, the highest point of the hill, hosts the remains of a Romano-Celtic temple built in the late 3rd century AD, in use until the early 5th century [1] [2]. A burial ground with 16 graves lies north of the temple, and a sunken chamber to the south showed marks of burning [2] [3] [4].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236617", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: lat ''51.118409868462685'' -> ''51.1282''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:236618", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s003: lon ''-2.47207381629472'' -> ''-2.47845''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247433", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247434", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385101", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385102", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('39461539-85ee-47d9-9f64-b6a6587844ec'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:39461539-85ee-47d9-9f64-b6a6587844ec:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''7'' restored on Spartia Temple', '5cdd7ee857c17d18ca312c1fcc608a54', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Temple complex'', ''Undated'') is shared by 11 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82852", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2073:chunk-0001: description ''The Spartia Temple is an ancient Greek sanctuary at the foot of Spartia hill, north of Sesklo in the Magnesia region of Thessaly. A bronze omphalos phiale bearing an archaic inscription dedicated by Tilephilos to Heracles confirmed the site as the only excavated sanctuary of Heracles worship outside a city in the region of ancient Pherae. Discovered during natural gas pipeline construction in 1999, the site yielded bronze vases, weapons, figurines, black-figured roof tiles, and a Hellenistic phase built atop the earlier archaic sanctuary. Finds span from the Archaic through Byzantine periods.'' -> ''The Spartia temple is an ancient Greek cult site excavated at the foot of the hill of Spartia, north of the village of Sesklo, in the Magnesia regional unit of Greece [1]. An inscribed dedication suggests the worship there of the Greek mythological figures Heracles and Alcmene [1]. Items recovered include bronze vases, objects of lead and clay, weapons, iron tools, and figurines [1]. Some specific artifacts named are clay metopes with yellow veneer, spearheads, and part of the arm of a marble statue [1]. One important artifact is a bronze phiale in excellent condition with the inscription \"Tilephilos dedicated me to Herakles\" in the archaic Greek alphabet [1]. This indicates the presence of a Herakles cult, which is linked to Pherae and is documented in the region through Hellenistic-era inscriptions [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116195", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116196", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247437", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247438", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348084", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348085", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
