lt into a dry stone wall, and may have once formed a stone pair with the Longstone [1]. The area has numerous barrows and near the Longstone ornaments, flint and arrowheads have all been found [1]. The stone was believed to be able to cure infants of maladies such as measles and whooping cough, by passing the child through one of the natural holes [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97227", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97228", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247781", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247782", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357141", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357142", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-1600''"}]'::jsonb),
