the hill fort went into decline and became concentrated at the eastern end of the site [1]. It was occupied until at least the Roman period, by which time it was in the territory of the Durotriges, a Celtic tribe [1]. After the Roman conquest of Britain in the 1st century AD, Maiden Castle appears to have been abandoned, although the Romans may have had a military presence on the site [1]. In the late 4th century AD, a temple and ancillary buildings were constructed [1]. In about 450 BC, Maiden Castle was expanded from 6.4 to 19 ha [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35734", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-600'' -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147092", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/39a50b0a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/39a50b0a/Maiden_castle_dorset_ramparts.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
