rocks [1]. This caused the formation of many mineral deposits that were mined extensively in the 18th and early 19th centuries [1]. East Kit Hill Mine was worked from 1855 to 1909 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116289", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116290", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-4500'' -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116291", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: site_type ''Fortification'' -> ''Barrow''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116292", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kit_Hill'' -> ''https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=61289''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147832", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/411cacb0/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/411cacb0/Chimney on Kit Hill (3120).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
