 unproven [1]. Pottery found on site has been Roman or later in date [1]. The current earthworks appear to demonstrate a Norman motte and bailey castle of considerable natural strength [1]. The motte, now severely mutilated by later quarrying, measures approximately 52 metres in diameter by 3 metres high, and its ditch is 2.3 metres deep [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98098", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98099", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:148590", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/48130c20/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/48130c20/Bincknoll Castle - panoramio - ian freeman (1).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248243", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248244", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:310377", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/48130c20/Bincknoll Castle - panoramio - ian freeman (1).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/48130c20/Bincknoll geograph-958260-by-Brian-Robert-Marshall.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348189", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348190", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
