truscan tomb within Tumulo II at the Banditaccia Necropolis in Cerveteri, Italy, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The tomb is named for its carved stone funerary beds that distinguish between sexes: women''s beds feature triangular raised sections at both ends, while men''s beds adopt the klinal (couch) form. In dual burials, the husband was placed on the left side and the wife on the right when viewed from the entrance. The necropolis spans 400 hectares and contains about 1,000 tombs dating from the 9th century BC.\" -> \"The Tomb of Funeral Beds (Tomba dei Letti Funebri) is a 6th-century BC Etruscan tomb within Tumulo II at the Banditaccia Necropolis in Cerveteri, Italy, a UNESCO World Heritage Site [1] [2]. The tomb is named for its carved stone funerary beds that distinguish between sexes: women''s beds feature triangular raised sections, while men''s beds adopt the klinal (couch) form [1] [3] [4].\""}]'::jsonb),
    ('4d0928dd-8050-4e45-a9d2-f9a8331fa425'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:4d0928dd-8050-4e45-a9d2-f9a8331fa425:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''5'' restored on Saraakallio Rock Paintings', '5bf45fd1a4f3a39360c1dcd9f9d49ac7', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Rock art'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 19 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:83770", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2085:chunk-0001: description \"The Saraakallio Rock Paintings are prehistoric petroglyphs in Central Finland, dating to 4500–3000 BC [1]. Located on the eastern shore of Lake Saraavesi in Laukaa, the site features two distinct art areas—Saraakallio I and Saraakallio II—on a prominent cliff face overlooking the Keitele Canal [1]. The paintings depict elk, humans, and abstract symbols, representing some of Finland''s oldest surviving rock art [1].\" -> ''Saraakallio rock paintings are situated on the Saraakallio cliff in Laukaa, Central Finland [1]. The rock site lies on the eastern shore of Lake Saraavesi [1]. An important water route, the Keitele Canal, runs in front of the paintings [1]. There are two art areas, Saraakallio I and Saraakallio II [1]. It is difficult to count and list all the paintings of Saraakallio, partly because they are so many and varied, and also because many of them are blurred, fragmentary or have been painted over [1]. The pictures number between 50–200, making it the biggest rock art area in Finland [1]. The oldest paintings are circa 6,600 years old [1]. The most common themes in Saraakallio paintings are deer, human, and boat figures [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98167", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98168", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149408", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3d/Laukaa_-_rock_painting2.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/4d0928dd/Kalliomaalaukset Saraakalliolla.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237568", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237569", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-5000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:310451", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/4d0928dd/Kalliomaalaukset Saraakalliolla.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/4d0928dd/Laukaa_-_rock_painting2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
