, "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4307:chunk-0001: description \"The Tsagaan Salaa rock paintings comprise one of the largest rock art complexes in North and Central Asia, located in western Mongolia''s Altai Tavan Bogd National Park. Spanning roughly 15 square kilometres along the White River Valley, the site contains over 10,000 figures dating from the Neolithic (c. 11,000 BC) through the Bronze Age to the Turkic period. Imagery documents the transition from big-game hunting to pastoral herding and horse-dependent nomadism. Inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2011 as part of the Petroglyphic Complexes of the Mongolian Altai.\" -> ''The Tsagaan Salaa rock paintings comprise one of the largest rock art complexes in North and Central Asia [1]. Spanning roughly 15 square kilometres along the White River Valley, the site contains over 10,000 figures [2] [3] [4]. Imagery documents the transition from big-game hunting to pastoral herding and horse-dependent nomadism [3] [5]. Inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2011 as part of the Petroglyphic Complexes of the Mongolian Altai [3] [5].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385745", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385746", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4dc7086c-f261-4f38-85f2-10a20eeda1bc'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:4dc7086c-f261-4f38-85f2-10a20eeda1bc:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''5'' restored on La Garma Cave Complex', '2f05f633be4a343d17c344d882ccd22a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Rock art'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 19 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44359", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0091:chunk-0001: description ''The La Garma Cave Complex is a parietal art-bearing paleoanthropological cave system in Cantabria, Spain, located just north of the village of Omoño in the municipality of Ribamontán al Monte [1]. The cave complex contains more than 4,000 fossils and over 500 graphical units, including 109 signs, 92 animal figures, and 40 hand stencils [2]. It is noted for having one of the best preserved floors from the Paleolithic period in Europe [1]. La Garma is part of the Cave of Altamira and Paleolithic Cave Art of Northern Spain World Heritage Site [1].'' -> ''The La Garma cave complex is a parietal art-bearing paleoanthropological cave system in Cantabria, Spain [1]. The cave complex is noted for one of the best preserved floors from the Paleolithic containing more than 4,000 fossils and more than 500 graphical units [1]. The Lower Gallery of La Garma is situated at 59 m above sea level and is around 300 m in length [1]. It was discovered in November 1995 [1]. Its original entrance was sealed during the Pleistocene by a rockslide about 16,000 years ago, preserving the cave floor in a pristine manner [1]. La Garma is notable for its rich repository of Magdalenian portable art found in The Lower Gallery [1]. The most outstanding artefact is a backward-facing ibex depiction carved onto a bovine rib spatula [1]. The peculiar remains of five Visigothic youths were found deep in the cave system [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149418", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/4dc7086c/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/4dc7086c/Sepultura mesolítica de la cueva de ''El Truchiro'', en Ribamontán al Monte.webp\""}]'::jsonb),
