he cave floor in a pristine manner [1]. La Garma is notable for its rich repository of Magdalenian portable art found in The Lower Gallery [1]. The most outstanding artefact is a backward-facing ibex depiction carved onto a bovine rib spatula [1]. The peculiar remains of five Visigothic youths were found deep in the cave system [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149418", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/4dc7086c/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/4dc7086c/Sepultura mesolítica de la cueva de ''El Truchiro'', en Ribamontán al Monte.webp\""}]'::jsonb),
