ediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4309:chunk-0001: description \"The Lia Fáil (Stone of Destiny) is a megalithic stone on the Hill of Tara''s Inauguration Mound in County Meath, Ireland, used as the coronation seat for the King of Tara and High King of Ireland [1]. Legend claims all Irish kings were crowned on this stone until Muirchertach mac Ercae c. 500 AD [1]. The stone was believed to possess magical properties, notably ''screaming'' when a rightful king stood upon it [1].\" -> \"The Lia Fáil (Stone of Destiny) is a megalithic stone on the Hill of Tara''s Inauguration Mound in County Meath, Ireland [1] [2] [3]. Legend claims all Irish kings were crowned on this stone until Muirchertach mac Ercae c. 500 AD [1]. The stone was believed to possess magical properties [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348255", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348256", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('53058d01-7e64-49c7-8dec-2b352a0e9ec6'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:53058d01-7e64-49c7-8dec-2b352a0e9ec6:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''4'' restored on Grey Croft Stone Circle', '38a685a37bb5d65bd9d2dece79c97267', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Stone circle'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 37 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84350", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2088:chunk-0001: description ''Grey Croft is a Bronze Age stone circle near Seascale in Cumbria, measuring approximately 30 metres in diameter with 10 surviving stones of an original 12, some reaching nearly two metres high. The stones are hard agglomerates of the Borrowdale volcanic series, with one outlier at 34 metres distance. In 1820, farmer James Fox buried all but one stone to clear his fields; in 1949, W. Fletcher and boys from Pelham House School unearthed and restored them. Excavations yielded Bronze Age flints, stone axes, a Whitby jet ring, and red granite cobbles from a burial cairn.'' -> ''Grey Croft stone circle is a restored stone circle near Seascale in Cumbria [1]. Grey Croft stone circle is a circle of 12 stones situated south of the Sellafield nuclear site [1]. Only 10 of the original 12 stones are currently standing [1]. The stones in the circle were toppled over and buried in 1820 by a tenant farmer, with the exception of one stone [1]. In 1949 the site was excavated and nine of the stones were located, and replaced as accurately as possible [1]. The excavations uncovered an oval stone cairn situated in the circle centre [1]. Trenching under the cairn revealed charcoal traces, calcined bones, a broken early Bronze Age jet or lignite ring, and flint flakes and scraper [1]. A Great Langdale Late-Neolithic stone axe was found near to the eastern stone of the circle [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98901", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98902", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248327", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248328", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348259", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348260", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2900''"}]'::jsonb),
