    ('543e7a38-517f-42d2-a716-172e35c434fa'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:543e7a38-517f-42d2-a716-172e35c434fa:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Coxall Knoll', 'b81aed5b66b647e75b84bf7b8303e584', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(52.35545068563179, -2.9333570873843358, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84386", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2089:chunk-0001: description ''Coxall Knoll is an Iron Age hillfort on the Shropshire-Herefordshire border, encompassing roughly 12 acres across three enclosures with up to three ramparts and two ditches on its northern side. The oval hillfort at 262m elevation features inturned rampart entrances and wide quarry ditches. It faces Brandon Camp hillfort across the River Teme, with three Roman camps in the valley between them, indicating the area remained strategically important into the Roman period. Interior deposits likely contain post holes, hearths, and storage pits revealing Iron Age occupation.'' -> ''Coxall Knoll is a hill lying on the boundary of Shropshire and Herefordshire, England; it is near Bucknell in Shropshire and Buckton and Coxall in Herefordshire [1]. On the summit is an Iron Age hillfort, a scheduled monument [1]. The height of the hill is 262 metres and it has a prominence of 120 metres [1]. The hillfort on the summit is roughly oval in shape, measuring about 570 metres west to east and 200 metres north to south [1]. There are earthen banks following the contours of the hill; the slopes below have been made steeper by the builders of the fort [1]. The main enclosure, with three banks and ditches to the north, has an area of about 3 hectares [1]. Adjoining is a roughly triangular eastern enclosure with an area of about 1.8 hectares, and an enclosure to the north of this with an area of about 0.7 hectares [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98919", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98920", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248337", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248338", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s007: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385762", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385763", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
