e today is not the original Archaic structure but rather a medieval reconstruction, likely dating to the 13th-14th century, which incorporated the ancient spolia and relief into its design [1]. The site reflects successive phases of occupation and rebuilding spanning from the 6th century BC through the 5th century AD [1].'' -> ''The site reflects successive phases of occupation and rebuilding [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349010", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349011", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
