oking the Wylye valley about 1 km northeast of Norton Bavant in Wiltshire, England. The fort covers 15 hectares (37 acres) and occupies the summit of the hill on the edge of Salisbury Plain. Its four-sided earthworks follow the natural contours of the hilltop, enclosing one of the larger hillforts in Wiltshire.[1]'' -> ''Scratchbury Camp is an Iron Age univallate hillfort on Scratchbury Hill, overlooking the Wylye valley about 1 km northeast of Norton Bavant in Wiltshire, England [1]. The fort occupies the summit of the hill on the edge of Salisbury Plain [1]. Its four-sided earthworks follow the natural contours of the hilltop [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345680", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345681", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('574b24e0-9357-4d1a-a66b-556a0dfe6303'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:574b24e0-9357-4d1a-a66b-556a0dfe6303:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Cadbury Hill', '13d8af4097a4e699e9f697490bbe3c6e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(51.380537291713374, -2.8032672911453447, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28295", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0107:chunk-0001: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30407", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43529", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0075:chunk-0001: description \"Iron Age hillfort atop Cadbury Hill near Congresbury in North Somerset, known archaeologically as Cadbury-Congresbury to distinguish it from the Somerset Cadbury Castle. The fort enclosed roughly 8.5 acres with ramparts, walls, and ditches, and was abandoned during the Roman occupation. Uniquely, it was substantially reoccupied in the post-Roman ''Dark Age'' (c. 400-700 AD), when Mediterranean amphorae imports and evidence of a turf-and-timber watchtower, timber hall, and continued Byzantine trade were discovered, suggesting a settlement of considerable importance.\" -> ''Cadbury Hill is a small hill, mostly in the civil parish of Congresbury, overlooking the village of Yatton in North Somerset [1]. On its summit stands an Iron Age hill fort, which is a Scheduled Ancient Monument [1]. In archaeological circles, the hill fort is known as Cadbury-Congresbury in order to differentiate it from the Cadbury Castle hillfort in South Cadbury [1]. It appears to have been constructed in the Iron Age when one or more ramparts, with walls and ditches, were built on the steep slopes of the hill to defend an area covering some eight and a half acres [1]. The remains of Iron Age round houses may still be seen inside [1]. The hill fort was refortified around 400, after the urban collapse associated with the withdrawal of Rome, and occupation extended into the sub-Roman period [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117601", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117602", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117603", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150194", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/574b24e0/hero.webp'' -> ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/ST4464_Ancient_Hill_Fort%2C_Cadbury_Hill_-_geograph.org.uk_-_68763.jpg''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248723", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248724", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333832", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/ST4464_Ancient_Hill_Fort%2C_Cadbury_Hill_-_geograph.org.uk_-_68763.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/574b24e0/View_from_Cadbury_Hill.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385768", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385769", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
