6-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/589b9ba5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/589b9ba5/Dundon Camp Somerset Map.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248735", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248736", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:337397", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4311:chunk-0001: description ''Dundon Hill Hillfort is a univallate Iron Age hillfort in Compton Dundon, Somerset, England, designated as a Scheduled Ancient Monument. Situated above the River Cary overlooking the Somerset Levels, the outer earthworks enclose approximately 4.8 hectares. A 1997 water pipeline excavation through the rampart revealed a multi-phase defensive sequence: an initial timber-laced stone rampart that was subsequently burned, overlaid by a later clay rampart, with possible pre-rampart cobbles suggesting earlier occupation. Earlier surface finds from 1916 included flint tools and Bronze Age pottery. Southeast of the fort lies a Bronze Age bowl barrow possibly modified as a Norman motte, known as Dundon Beacon. The defenses suggest dating from the Late Bronze Age to Early Iron Age (8th-5th centuries BC), though quarrying that ended in 1925 significantly altered the site.'' -> ''Dundon Hill Hillfort is a univallate Iron Age hillfort in Compton Dundon, Somerset, England, designated as a Scheduled Ancient Monument [1] [2]. Situated overlooking the Somerset Levels, the outer earthworks enclose approximately 4.8 hectares [3]. A 1997 water pipeline excavation through the rampart revealed a multi-phase defensive sequence: an initial timber-laced stone rampart that was subsequently burned, overlaid by a later clay rampart, with possible pre-rampart cobbles suggesting earlier occupation [2]. Earlier surface finds from 1916 included flint tools and Bronze Age pottery [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385770", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385771", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
