position approximately 185 metres (607 ft) above sea level, overlooking the town of Sidbury and the River Sid valley below. [1] Dating to the Iron Age period (approximately 500-1500 BC), the fortification represents a significant example of prehistoric defensive architecture in South West England. [1] The site features defensive earthworks and occupies a strategic location commanding panoramic views over the surrounding landscape. [1]'' -> ''Sidbury Castle is a substantial Iron Age hill fort situated near Sidbury in Devon, England [1]. The fortress occupies a hilltop position approximately 185 metres (607 ft) above sea level, overlooking the town of Sidbury and the River Sid valley below [1] [2]. The site features defensive earthworks [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385780", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385781", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('59af6742-7a6d-45ba-9cb7-9fd0de0c51c9'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:59af6742-7a6d-45ba-9cb7-9fd0de0c51c9:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''7'' restored on Casma-Sechin Culture', 'fe63455c6d31dbc13fac3e475c7afbd2', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Archaeological site'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 5 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43531", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0075:chunk-0001: description ''The Casma-Sechin culture (c. 3600-200 BC) encompasses a large concentration of prehistoric ruins in the Casma and Sechin river valleys of coastal Peru. Sechin Bajo, with a circular plaza radiocarbon-dated to 3500 BC, may contain the oldest monumental architecture in the Americas. Sechin Alto, a flat-topped pyramid measuring 300x250m and 35m high, was the largest construction in the Americas when built around 1600-1400 BC. Cerro Sechin, discovered in 1937 by Julio C. Tello, features megalithic walls with bas-relief carvings graphically depicting human sacrifice. The size and uniformity of these monuments suggest Sechin Alto served as the administrative center of a polity uniting the valleys under one government.'' -> ''The Casma–Sechin culture (c. 3600 BCE–200 BCE) of Peru refers to the large concentration of pre-historic ruins in the valleys of the Casma River and its tributary the Sechin River and along the nearby coast of the Pacific Ocean [1]. The ruins include major archaeological sites such as Sechin Bajo, Sechin Alto, Cerro Sechin, Mojeque, Chankillo, and Taukachi-Konkan, as well as other smaller sites [1]. Most of these inland sites are found in the river valleys about 20 kilometres distant from the ocean [1]. The seaside sites of Huaynuná and Las Haldas are found about 20 kilometres north and south of the mouth of the Casma River on the coast [1]. The area of the Casma/Sechin culture extended about 40 kilometres inland from the sea [1]. By 3000 BC, at a few locations in coastal Peru, including the Casma/Sechin valleys, a sizable population was present and undertaking large projects such as building pyramids and other ceremonial and monumental structures [1]. Radiocarbon dating indicates a plaza at Sechin Bajo was constructed in 3500 BCE [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117647", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150314", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/59af6742/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/59af6742/Frontis_Templo_Sechin.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311235", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/59af6742/Frontis_Templo_Sechin.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/59af6742/Sechín_Archaeological_site_-_relief_(head_profile_left).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
