, Sechin Alto, Cerro Sechin, Mojeque, Chankillo, and Taukachi-Konkan, as well as other smaller sites [1]. Most of these inland sites are found in the river valleys about 20 kilometres distant from the ocean [1]. The seaside sites of Huaynuná and Las Haldas are found about 20 kilometres north and south of the mouth of the Casma River on the coast [1]. The area of the Casma/Sechin culture extended about 40 kilometres inland from the sea [1]. By 3000 BC, at a few locations in coastal Peru, including the Casma/Sechin valleys, a sizable population was present and undertaking large projects such as building pyramids and other ceremonial and monumental structures [1]. Radiocarbon dating indicates a plaza at Sechin Bajo was constructed in 3500 BCE [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117647", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Archaeological site''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150314", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/59af6742/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/59af6742/Frontis_Templo_Sechin.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311235", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/59af6742/Frontis_Templo_Sechin.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/59af6742/Sechín_Archaeological_site_-_relief_(head_profile_left).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('59c0ea5b-ba27-4a21-afdf-b4ec1ab0aa69'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:59c0ea5b-ba27-4a21-afdf-b4ec1ab0aa69:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''6'' restored on Pont Flavien', 'd7217daaced01429d12598675ffcbf2a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Gate/archway/bridge'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 26 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84676", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2093:chunk-0001: description ''The Pont Flavien is a single-arch Roman bridge spanning the River Touloubre in Saint-Chamas, southern France, built from limestone around 12 BC during the Augustan period [1]. It carried the Via Julia Augusta between Placentia, Italy and Arles [1]. It is the only surviving example of a Roman bridge bounded by triumphal arches from the Augustan period [1]. Similar bridges probably existed elsewhere, as indicated by portrayals on coins of the late 1st century BC [1].'' -> ''The Pont Flavien is a Roman bridge across the River Touloubre in Saint-Chamas, Bouches-du-Rhône department [1]. The single-arch crossing, which was built from limestone, was on a Roman road - the Via Julia Augusta - between Placentia, Italy and Arles [1]. It is the only surviving example of a Roman bridge bounded by triumphal arches from the Augustan period, although similar bridges probably existed elsewhere, as indicated by portrayals on coins of the late 1st century BC [1]. The bridge probably replaced an earlier wooden structure on the same site [1]. It measures 21.4 metres long by 6.2 metres wide [1]. The two arches at either end, each standing 7 metres high with a single wide bay, are constructed of the same local stone as the bridge and are broader than they are tall [1]. At the corners of the arches are fluted Corinthian pilasters at the top of which are carved eagles [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150315", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3a/Pont_Flavien%2C_Bouches-du-Rh%C3%B4ne%2C_France._Pic_02.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/59c0ea5b/Pont Flavien 20111216 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311238", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/59c0ea5b/Pont Flavien 20111216 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/59c0ea5b/Pont_Flavien,_Bouches-du-Rhône,_France._Pic_02.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
