ds (73 m) [1]. There is one surviving rampart, 2–3 feet (0.61–0.91 m) above the interior, and 10 feet (3.0 m) externally [1]. There are entrances on the west and east sides [1]. The rampart is surrounded by a belt of flat ground about 60 feet (18 m) wide and about 3 feet (0.91 m) high: aerial photographs show that this area was originally outer defences, since reduced by ploughing [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99979", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99980", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150910", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f1/Padderbury_Top_-_geograph.org.uk_-_171437.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5c3a138c/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248785", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248786", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349060", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349061", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354777", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354778", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_start None -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
