ive stone circles known from this area, on the borders between Shropshire and Powys [1]. Of these, only the Hoarstones and Mitchell''s Fold survive [1]. The Hoarstones contains between 38 and 40 stones, arranged in an elliptical fashion [1]. Just south of the centre of the circle is a single stone, measuring around 1 metre (3 feet) high; it is unclear if this is an original prehistoric feature of the monument or a later addition [1]. Around 1897, a Mr Jarrett ploughed up a perforated sandstone axe-head from the field immediately to the south of the circle [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99992", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99993", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248795", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248796", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349068", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349069", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}]'::jsonb),
