    ('5d8cbd90-1826-4ab0-b44f-94574d7dccc4'::uuid, 'mystery', '9', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:5d8cbd90-1826-4ab0-b44f-94574d7dccc4:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''8'' restored on Fountain of the Idol', '9139a590e0a6c1dd0e015f42d8f93f14', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 9 from (''Sanctuary'', ''1 - 500 AD'') is shared by 2 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84798", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2096:chunk-0001: description ''The Fountain of the Idol (Fonte do Idolo) is a 1st-century Roman granite fountain in Braga, northern Portugal, built within the territory of ancient Bracara Augusta. Commissioned by Celicus Fronto, a Roman citizen from Arcobriga, the monument bears Latin inscriptions dedicating it to the indigenous deities Tongoenabiagus and Nabia, reflecting a syncretic water cult. Its uniqueness led to classification as a Portuguese National Monument in 1910. Between 2001-2004, major musealization works added a protective structure enabling public access, while excavations by the University of Minho uncovered Roman drainage canals and wall structures.'' -> ''The Fountain of the Idol is a Roman fountain located in the civil parish of São José de São Lázaro, in the municipality of Braga, northern Portugal [1]. Located in the former territory of the Callaici Bracari, the granite rock fountain/spring has Latin inscriptions, dedicated to the Gallaecian and Lusitanian gods Tongoenabiagus and Nabia [1]. The construction of the fountain probably began in the 1st century, associated with a water cult, dedicated to the Lusitanian divinity Tongoenbiagus, and ordered constructed by Celicus Fronto [1]. The fountain is a large granite surface, forming an elongated backrest, measuring about 3 metres wide and 1.20 metres high [1]. On the left of the rock is a carved human figure, about 1.10 metres tall, upright, but deteriorated, and possibly male with a beard, wrapped in a toga, holding in his left arm a bulky object [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117691", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''Megalithic structures'' -> ''Sanctuary''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150976", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d8cbd90/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d8cbd90/Fonte do Idolo (10).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333865", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d8cbd90/Fonte do Idolo (10).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d8cbd90/Fonte_do_Ídolo_Braga.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
