ey Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty [1]. It is situated on the spur of a hill between Llangollen and Corwen, commanding the valley junction and fertile plain at the confluence of the River Dee and the River Alwen [1]. The earliest structure was a small enclosure built against a natural rock outcrop [1]. A later, larger fortress was surrounded by a dry-stone wall, probably derived from the abundant scree in the area, and does not have the earthen ramparts of other local hillforts [1]. Caer Drewyn is an Iron Age fort dating back to about 500 BC, however it was in use as a defensive position long after this [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100027", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100028", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151008", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5e5354ff/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5e5354ff/Bryngaer_Geltaidd_Caer_Drewyn_Celtic_Hillfort_near_Corwen,_from_the_air;_2023_35.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237711", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237712", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349082", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349083", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
