e original [1]. In 1999 a geophysical survey was carried out suggesting that Blackers Hill originated as a univallate structure and was then later modified, forming a developed hill fort [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100071", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100072", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249191", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249192", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385808", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385809", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
