    ('61d2ef8c-e4a4-4dca-b7e7-36d58f391b60'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:61d2ef8c-e4a4-4dca-b7e7-36d58f391b60:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Kelsey Head', '2b9579cb75c9db880e96d7119ac173b9', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(50.404627324190194, -5.146453647024064, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84896", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2099:chunk-0001: description ''Kelsey Head is a coastal Site of Special Scientific Interest (SSSI) and headland in north Cornwall, England, noted for its biological interest. The site contains an Iron Age hill fort, a 170 by 160 metre cliff castle with earthwork remains dating to 500-300 BC. Evidence of earlier Mesolithic and Neolithic habitation has been found through flint flake discoveries not related to the later fortification.'' -> ''Kelsey Head is a coastal Site of Special Scientific Interest and headland in north Cornwall, England [1]. The site contains an Iron Age hill fort [1]. The headland is the site of earthwork remains of a 170-metre by 160-metre cliff castle, dated to the Iron Age [1]. But there is evidence of earlier habitation on the site, of Mesolithic and Neolithic periods, through the discovery of flint flakes not related to the cliff castle [1]. The cliff castle features evidence of earth and stone ramparts, a smaller annexe and an earthwork and external ditch protecting the south-eastern, inland, side [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:1