est which connected the two wings [1]. The site was subsequently excavated by the antiquarians John Henry Middleton and William Bazeley [1]. Finds from the excavations included a silver-plated bronze bowl, a large number of 3rd- and 4th-century coins, samian ware pottery, iron knives and tools [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100859", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100860", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151759", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/55/Roman_villa_%283%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3081292.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/67bb2bbe/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249255", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249256", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331804", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/67bb2bbe/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/67bb2bbe/Roman villa (3) - geograph.org.uk - 3081292.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385834", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385835", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''43'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
