e contained bone fragments, pottery and charcoal [1]. Also found were two Anglo-Saxon burials which had been cut into the top of the existing mound [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100929", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100930", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249657", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249658", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312172", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6c689af9/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6c689af9/Lyneham Longbarrow - geograph.org.uk - 3144.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385844", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385845", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6c6bb00c-45f8-4d2e-8532-79e612ae267a'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:6c6bb00c-45f8-4d2e-8532-79e612ae267a:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''6'' restored on Menhir of Bulhoa', '840b593234dde1990e89dfc09dc9d8df', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Megalithic stones'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 9 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29528", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0302:chunk-0001: period_start ''-4500'' -> ''-3500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34875", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0035:chunk-0001: description ''A granite megalithic standing stone near Monsaraz in Reguengos de Monsaraz, Evora district, Portugal, dating to approximately 4000-2500 BC. Originally 4 metres tall, it was only identified in 1970 when found lying flat and fractured. After restoration it was re-erected, though it lost its original base which had to be recarved. Classified as a National Monument since 1970, the menhir features engraved circles and lines of uncertain meaning.'' -> \"The Menhir of Bulhoa (Portuguese: Menir da Bulhoa), also known as the Menhir of Abelhoa, is a granite megalithic standing stone, located near the parish of Monsaraz, in the municipality of the Reguengos de Monsaraz, in the Évora district of the Alentejo region of Portugal [1]. The menhir is thought to date back to between 3500 and 2500 BCE [1]. Overlooked for a long time, it was identified in 1970 [1]. At that time it was lying flat on the ground, with the upper part separated from its base, which had been used in a nearby grape press [1]. It was restored to its original shape soon after discovery, with the fracture remaining very noticeable [1]. The menhir is part of a megalithic nucleus that includes the menhirs of Monte da Ribeira and Outeiro and the Xerez Cromlech [1]. It has a phallic appearance, being about four meters high and one meter in diameter [1]. The stone is decorated with engravings depicting the sun''s rays, a staff, and wavy and zigzagging lines [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35820", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-3500'' -> ''-4500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152309", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6c6bb00c/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6c6bb00c/Menir da Bulhoa Reguengos de Monsaraz 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312175", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/6c6bb00c/Menir da Bulhoa Reguengos de Monsaraz 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6c6bb00c/BulhoaMenhir1.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
