    ('6d04a9ad-3da8-415b-a69a-2f3343244e67'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '1', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:6d04a9ad-3da8-415b-a69a-2f3343244e67:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''1'' restored on Castro of Monte Castelo', '3f70165689492c5b98c30b20ce15c839', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 86 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34903", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0036:chunk-0001: description ''The Castro of Monte Castelo is a fortified settlement in Guifoes, Matosinhos, on a hillside beside the Leca River in northern Portugal, covering approximately 8 hectares. Occupied continuously from before the 5th century BC through the 5th century AD, it saw significant development from the 1st century onward following integration into the Roman Empire. Defended by three lines of walls, the site includes a temple on the upper level, a ceramic oven, and a necropolis. Excavations since 2016 with the University of Porto revealed 1st-century house ruins and imported artifacts from southern Spain, Italy, and North Africa. Classified as a Property of Public Interest since 1971, the municipality acquired 80% of the site in 2024 for expanded research.'' -> ''The Castro of Monte Castelo is a Calcolithic fortified settlement, situated in the civil parish of Custóias, Leça do Balio e Guifões, in the municipality of Matosinhos in the northern Portuguese district of Porto [1]. In 1878, there were archaeological excavations under the direction of Francisco Martins Sarmento [1]. The site is situated on the periphery of Guifões, on the eastern flank of a hilltop overlooking the town, surrounded by pine forests, overlooking the Leça River [1]. The fortified settlement is defended by three lines of walls [1]. On the western flank, the area has been excavated, resulting in the unearthing of family homes of circular and rectangular plans [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118915", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: lat ''41.20015334932948'' -> ''41.200405''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118916", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: lon ''-8.6299892745146'' -> ''-8.678481''"}]'::jsonb),
