ance is on the west side [1]. There is a circular mound outside the entrance: it is not an earlier barrow, but may be a defensive feature [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100986", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249689", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249690", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385854", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385855", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
