8262", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4322:chunk-0001: description \"The Station Stones are four sarsen stones erected at Stonehenge during its second or third phase, around 2640-2480 BCE, forming the corners of a precise rectangle straddling the inner stone circle. Only two of the original four stones survive today. Two stood on earth mounds called the North and South barrows, though these never contained burials. The rectangular alignment mirrors the monument''s solstitial axis and may also mark lunar alignments, making these stones significant for understanding the astronomical planning of Stonehenge.\" -> \"The Station Stones are four sarsen stones erected at Stonehenge forming the corners of a precise rectangle straddling the inner stone circle [1] [2] [3]. Only two of the original four stones survive today [1] [2]. Two stood on earth mounds called the North and South barrows, though these never contained burials [1]. The rectangular alignment mirrors the monument''s solstitial axis and may also mark lunar alignments [3].\""}]'::jsonb),
    ('72cd16e3-8fc7-49a6-8f6d-efc56c40508d'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:72cd16e3-8fc7-49a6-8f6d-efc56c40508d:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: antiquity ''7'' restored on Crawley Edge Cairns', '17277305560177f823c2adf640293607', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34941", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0037:chunk-0001: description ''The Crawley Edge Cairns are a group of 42 Bronze Age round barrows, cairns, and clearance cairns on a south-facing slope in Crawleyside, near Stanhope, County Durham. Ranging from 1.8m to 8.5m in diameter and 0.2m to 1m high, many retain traces of surrounding kerbs. Excavations in the 1970s dated the site to 2000-1500 BC and uncovered a collared urn containing cremated bone, three jet beads, flint tools, and charcoal. The inclusion of clearance cairns alongside burial cairns indicates agricultural land clearance alongside funerary practices. Cairnfields are uncommon in County Durham, making this a notable example.'' -> ''The Crawley Edge Cairns are a series of forty-two Bronze Age round barrows, cairns and clearance cairns located in a field in Crawleyside, near Stanhope, County Durham, England [1]. The cairnfield site lies on a gentle south-facing slope of a hill-spur in Weardale and remains in open moorland [1]. Two of the cairns were excavated in 1977 and surveys undertaken in 1984 and 1991 [1]. The inclusion of clearance cairns at the site is usually taken as an indication of clearance in advance of arable farming, but the Crawley Edge field unusually includes a barrow cremation mound among the cairns [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101686", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101687", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249723", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249724", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385862", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385863", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-2500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
