Murujuga are an Aboriginal nation known as the Yaburara people [1]. Some of the Aboriginal rock carvings have been dated to more than 45,000 years old, and some of the collection is generally estimated to be 40,000–50,000 years old [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118986", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''Rock art'' -> ''Petroglyphs''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s005: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murujuga'' -> ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burrup_Peninsula''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152974", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-016: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a9/Pilbara_Billabong.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7356fc90/Ancient_and_Modern_4,000_years.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:334532", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7356fc90/Ancient_and_Modern_4,000_years.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7356fc90/Pilbara_Billabong.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
