    ('73be8eb3-140a-4646-8bfa-e7ec9d78c38c'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:73be8eb3-140a-4646-8bfa-e7ec9d78c38c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''6'' restored on Peñas de Cabrera', 'bde492b7e2de56987f4ebafab4b08dbc', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Rock art'', ''Undated'') is shared by 31 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85330", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2111:chunk-0001: description ''The archaeological site Peñas de Cabrera contains numerous rock shelters with prehistoric rock art, located in the municipality of Casabermeja, Spain [1]. The site features both paintings and engravings across its mountain and valley complex [1]. The surrounding area of Las Peñas de Cabrera is named after a district of the same name and is rich in natural minerals, rocks, and fossils [1].'' -> ''The archaeological site Peñas de Cabrera, containing numerous rock shelters, is located in the municipality of Casabermeja [1]. In the early 1970s the University of Málaga began research in Peñas de Cabrera, focusing particularly on its rock and cave paintings [1]. As of 2016 thirty-two rock shelters featuring paintings, engravings and archaeological material, mainly ceramic and flint, have been recorded [1]. The rock and cave art is found in shelters made of sandstone [1]. Bowl and cup engravings have also been discovered outside the shelters, on horizontal surface areas [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:118989", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2