, however, though it lost its political importance, still retained religious importance, for it contained two ancient and much revered sanctuaries – one of Athena, hence called the Lindian, and the other of Heracles [1]. The former was believed to have been built by Danaus, or, according to others by his daughters on their flight from Egypt [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101700", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101701", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152979", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-016: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/73ebc428/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/73ebc428/1016 Temple of Athena Lindia at Rhodes Photo by Giles Laurent.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249733", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249734", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349947", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349948", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-1500'' -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385866", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385867", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-6500''"}]'::jsonb),
