[1]. During the Iron Age and Roman era, the site was in the area of the Iceni tribe [1]. Holkham Camp is one of two possible sites corresponding to the description by the Roman historian Tacitus of the location of the defeat in AD 47 of Iceni rebels by a Roman force commanded by Ostorius Scapula [1]. The site may have been a feature in Mesolithic and Neolithic times, since finds include worked flints from these periods; they are thought to have been in their original location, as the site has not been ploughed [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101813", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101814", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153722", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-017: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7968021c/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7968021c/Holkham_Camp_Digital_Terrain_Model.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250141", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250142", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385892", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385893", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
