    ('7c94cfe0-8dc8-4286-acf4-dc994bd79853'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:7c94cfe0-8dc8-4286-acf4-dc994bd79853:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Huntsham Castle', '5fcbbbf3c4a399d9e4068ede90387a7f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(50.97411481774243, -3.4250321893185363, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35013", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0039:chunk-0001: description ''Iron Age hillfort (c. 500-300 BC) in Devon, England, occupying a prominent hill 260m above sea level [1]. The sub-circular univallate enclosure spans approximately 150m in diameter, overlooking valleys of two tributaries to the River Lowman [1]. A surrounding rampart reaches up to 2.9m externally and 2.4m internally, with greater height on the northern side [1].'' -> ''Huntsham Castle, Devon, England is an Iron Age Hill fort enclosure near the village of Huntsham [1]. The monument includes a slight univallate hillfort situated on a prominent hill overlooking the valleys of two separate tributaries to the River Lowman [1]. The monument survives as a sub-circular enclosure, defining an area which slopes gently down to the south and measures approximately 150m in diameter [1]. It is clearly demarcated on all sides by a rampart which varies in height from 1m up to 2.4m internally, being generally of greater height on the northern side of the enclosure [1]. Externally this rampart is up to 2.9m high [1]. Surrounding the rampart is an outer ditch which measures up to 5.4m wide and 0.4m deep and this is visible on all sides of the monument, although it is predominantly preserved as a buried feature [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101863", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101864", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250161", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250162", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385898", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385899", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
