te from the Iron Age, possibly being a ceremonial site of the Tarentaisian culture (c. 725 BC–450 BC) [1]. The stone circle was partly restored in the 19th century [1]. In the Roman era, a temple dedicated to Jupiter was erected nearby along with a mansio serving travellers along the pass, and it is thought that Carthaginian general Hannibal used this route [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120169", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120170", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120171", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_St_Bernard_Pass'' -> ''https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cromlech_du_Petit-Saint-Bernard''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:141485", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-01a_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:141486", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-01a_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153843", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-017: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7c97de3a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7c97de3a/Col_du_Petit-Saint-Bernard_-_cromlech.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
