ries [1]. The archaeologists found no evidence of a chambered long barrow at the location, and suggested that the Coffin Stone might once have stood upright in the vicinity [1]. The antiquarian William Stukeley made note of the Coffin Stone in his posthumously published 1776 work Itinerarium Curiosum [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102522", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102523", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153886", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-017: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7d453e37/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7d453e37/Coffin Stone, Blue Bell Hill, Kent 02.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250175", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250176", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313092", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7d453e37/Coffin Stone, Blue Bell Hill, Kent 02.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7d453e37/Coffin_Stone,_Blue_Bell_Hill,_Kent_01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350016", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350017", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
