t of a Bronze Age farming settlement, and a barrow cemetery about a mile away to the north [1]. The site is at grid reference SU263423, to the south-west of the village of Quarley [1]. The Port Way Roman road passes just to the south of the hill [1]. The hill''s summit is at 172 metres above sea level [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102531", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102532", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250179", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250180", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386501", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386502", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
