    ('83659142-eb78-4e7a-bc65-94a54387ef42'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '1', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:83659142-eb78-4e7a-bc65-94a54387ef42:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''1'' restored on Castercliff', 'fd8f0eae8333bf1ee6a35d3219e412e8', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 86 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35095", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0041:chunk-0001: description ''Castercliff is an Iron Age multivallate hillfort near Nelson and Colne in Lancashire, England[1][2].'' -> ''Castercliff is an Iron Age multivallate hillfort situated close to the towns of Nelson and Colne in Lancashire, Northern England [1]. On the upper part of the hill, triple rubble ramparts up to 1.5 metres high, separated by ditches of similar depth, surround the site on all sides except the north [1]. On this side the defences consist mainly of a single rampart and ditch, but some short lengths of triple rampart and ditch are also found here [1]. The inner rampart may have been timber-laced and revetted with stone and enclosed an oval area measuring approximately 115 by 76 metres [1]. The summit of the hill is 280 metres above sea level and the surrounding ground falls rapidly on all sides except the south east [1]. The hillfort has been damaged by coal mining with old bell pits evident both inside and around the site [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:154574", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-018: thu