    ('89dd0394-47e5-479e-a2a7-6e78b3d7a267'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:89dd0394-47e5-479e-a2a7-6e78b3d7a267:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''4'' restored on Wittenham Clumps', '0ee390d5d7ad7f9e5915fefffb5488d0', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Fort'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 28 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81068", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2018:chunk-0001: description ''A pair of chalk hills in the Thames Valley featuring Castle Hill, an Iron Age hillfort with earliest earthworks from the Late Bronze Age. A large settlement at the foot of the hill housed several hundred people who farmed wheat, barley, and livestock. Excavations from 2019-2021 uncovered 15 Iron Age roundhouses, a vast Romano-British settlement, and thousands of finds including pottery, human skeletons, and spinning weights. The nearby Wittenham Sword (120 BC-AD 43) and an oval bronze shield were found in the adjacent River Isis.'' -> ''Wittenham Clumps are a pair of wooded chalk hills in the Thames Valley, in the civil parish of Little Wittenham, in the historic county of Berkshire, although since 1974 administered as part of South Oxfordshire district [1]. The higher of the two, Round Hill, is 390 feet above sea-level [1]. The 350-foot Castle Hill is about 380 yards south-east and was the site of an Iron Age hill fort [1]. The earliest earthworks date to the late Bronze Age [1]. More banks and ditches were added during the early Iron Age [1]. Excavation has revealed that the Iron Age inhabitants caught fish and wild boar as well as herding cattle and sheep [1]. There is also evidence of barley and wheat cultivation [1]. The fort appears to have been abandoned by the late Iron Age, the next occupants being Romans [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120307", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155295", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-019: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/39/Round_Hill%2C_Wittenham_Clumps.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/89dd0394/Round_Hill,_Wittenham_Clumps.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
