a Mycenaean tholos type tomb built in c. 1250 BC [1]. The Tomb of Clytemnestra with its imposing façade is together with the Treasury of Atreus the most monumental tomb of that type [1]. The entrance to the tomb consists of a dromos with walls of ashlar in conglomerate [1]. The exterior façade of the stomion is decorated with half-columns made of gypsum which were carefully carved with ornate capitals and vertical fluting [1]. A large relieving triangle overlaps the door lintel [1]. It was originally decorated by a colored relief sculpture [1]. Through the lintel block a small drain is cut in the rock, lined with low rubble walls and roofed with small slabs [1]. During the Ottoman rule of Greece the tomb was raided by Veli Pasha [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155301", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-019: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c1/20100408_mykines51.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8a30c67b/C3.22 »Grab der Klytemästra«, Drómos u. Eingang.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313898", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/8a30c67b/C3.22 »Grab der Klytemästra«, Drómos u. Eingang.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8a30c67b/20100408_mykines51.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
