ey \"Borgar dalr\" (valley of the fortress), referencing the ancient fort. An 18th-century slate quarry destroyed much of the southern fortification. The summit was given to the National Trust as a World War One memorial to Borrowdale\\''s fallen.'' -> ''Castle Crag is a hill in the North Western Fells of the English Lake District [1]. The wooded height of Castle Crag rises between Broadslack Gill and the Derwent [1]. The slopes of Castle Crag are extensively quarried with pits and levels on the northern and south eastern flanks [1]. The summit has also been extensively worked [1]. The summit area is believed to have been an ancient hill fort, although the western section has been sliced away by quarrying [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155336", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-019: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/8baf0d5a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8baf0d5a/Castle_crag.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250669", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250670", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313922", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/8baf0d5a/Castle_crag.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8baf0d5a/Castle_Crag_summit.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350842", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350843", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
