structure [1]. The original Roman bridge formed a part of the Via Augusta, and was the only bridge in the lower Llobregat valley until the 14th century [1]. It still features a Roman triumphal arch at its eastern abutment [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155382", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-019: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Pont_rom%C3%A0_%28Martorell_i_Castellbisbal%29_-_21.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8dec4979/Pont del Diable - entre més ponts.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/8dec4979/Pont del Diable - entre més ponts.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8dec4979/Pont_romà_(Martorell_i_Castellbisbal)_-_21.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
