circle to the north [1]. There are three other circles (or parts of circles) with alignments, one of which stretches for 18m [1]. Aubrey Burl considers the site to be typical of Irish Bronze Age ritual sites around the Sperrins, the local range of hills [1]. He argues that the layout of the stone circles and rows indicates connections with circle builders in England, Scotland and elsewhere in Northern Ireland [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103462", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103463", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251047", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251048", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350878", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350879", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386561", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386562", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-2500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
