ere are conspicuous gaps on the northern and western sides of the monument [1]. The site was rediscovered in 1898 and surveyed by the archaeologist Harold St George Gray in 1905 [1]. The site is 381 metres above sea level [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103490", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103491", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155942", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/Withypool_Stone_Circle_%28geograph_4591136%29.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/90cfd278/Withypool_Stone_Circle,_May_2014.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251067", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251068", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350896", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350897", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2350''"}]'::jsonb),
