 be seen in the north, west and south, most clearly in the north-west where it is 1 metre high and 14 metres wide [1]. The original entrance is thought to be in the south; its features are unclear because of sand and gravel extraction in recent times [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103525", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103526", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251075", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251076", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314023", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/923f9b29/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/923f9b29/View from Stafford Castle - geograph.org.uk - 1136249.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386571", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386572", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
