 the north is 10 metres wide [1]. As part of the Heather and Hillforts Project a topographic survey was commissioned, which took place between December 2006 and January 2007 [1]. The survey recorded the remains of 11 roundhouse platforms within the enclosure, concentrated on the eastern side [1]. In 2010 an archaeological excavation identified two roundhouses of about 7 metres diameter from different periods of occupation, and the results showed preservation of significant archaeological deposits in the interior of the hillfort, but also the fragile nature of the resource [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104190", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104191", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156016", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Moel_y_Gaer,_Llantysilio_Mountains_SSSI_and_Special_Areas_of_Conservation_in_Wales_-_2021_01.jpg/400px-Moel_y_Gaer,_Llantysilio_Mountains_SSSI_and_Special_Areas_of_Conservation_in_Wales_-_2021_01.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/931d37ed/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251091", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251092", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386579", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386580", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
