1]. The hill fort has an oval shape and is univallate [1]. The name \"Burrington Ham\" was commonly used for the hill fort before the 20th century [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104274", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104275", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156732", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/99685d28/hero.webp'' -> ''https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Burrington_Camp_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4876672.jpg/1280px-Burrington_Camp_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4876672.jpg''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251139", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251140", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:334630", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-002: thumbnail_url ''https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Burrington_Camp_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4876672.jpg/1280px-Burrington_Camp_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4876672.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/99685d28/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386601", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386602", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
