ons continued under the auspices of the Swedish Institute at Athens in the 1930s and then during the 1980s and 1990s that found two settlement areas on two different sides of the Mastos hill slope, belonging to the Early and Late Helladic periods, respectively [1]. They have found chamber tombs and large amounts of pottery that testify that the place was an important center of production of this material for many centuries [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121612", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121613", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:157543", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-022: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cb/Prosymna_Tholos_4.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9f99919a/Prosymna_Tholos_4.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251519", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251520", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350983", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350984", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''-800'' -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386623", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386624", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-6500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('9fe64aa7-1b1a-4074-b6c2-f2d236938ab4'::uuid, 'mystery', '2', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:9fe64aa7-1b1a-4074-b6c2-f2d236938ab4:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''6'' restored on Am Forsthofweg', '82805e9f94f5b93b5c3afab2b559c451', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 2 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''Undated'') is shared by 187 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:36995", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0048:chunk-0001: description ''(1st-2nd c. AD) Am Forsthofweg was a Roman castellum (small fort) situated along the Upper Germanic-Raetian Limes [1][2]. The site was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2005 as part of the \"Upper Germanic-Raetian Limes\" designation [2].'' -> ''The castellum or small fort nowadays called Am Forsthofweg was a Roman military camp of the Upper Germanic-Rhaetian Limes [1]. It received UNESCO World Heritage status in 2005 [1]. The fortification was located in the area of the current Bad Hönningen association of municipalities within the district of Neuwied in Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany [1]. The fort was discovered in 1894 under the direction of Heinrich Jacobi, the local section commissioner of the Imperial Limes Commission, and examined in two excavation campaigns in 1894 and 1901 [1]. The Roman fortlet \"Am Forsthofweg\" is an almost square earthwork [1]. A rampart and a ditch 5 meters wide and 1.5 meters deep served as a first defense line [1]. With its only gate, the camp faced north, towards the Limes frontline [1]. A wooden construction of unknown function, covering around 45 square meters was found inside [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105053", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105054", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251521", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251522", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:334648", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9fe64aa7/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9fe64aa7/Kleinkastell_am_Forsthofweg_3.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350985", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350986", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
