artian-language cuneiform inscription which states that Odzaberd was established by the Urartian king Rusa I (r. 735–714 BCE) in honor of the weather god Theispas to \"demonstrate the power of Biaina [the Urartian capital, modern Van] and to cow her enemies.\" Some sources refer to the site as \"Teisheba\" or other variations of the Urartian god\\''s name [1]. In the post-Urartian period Odzaberd was a regional center, as evidenced by recovered pottery styles and the use of mudbricks [1]. The Odzaberd site is on the southern shore of Lake Sevan near the town of Tsovinar [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121646", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: lat ''40.168024646758'' -> ''40.1528''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121647", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: lon ''45.45972198440738'' -> ''45.4953''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:157638", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-022: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/Overlooking_Teyseba.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a29d5e41/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325320", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a29d5e41/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a29d5e41/Overlooking Teyseba.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('a2b571fa-4aa3-4c23-b5f0-13c5552ce870'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '1', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:a2b571fa-4aa3-4c23-b5f0-13c5552ce870:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: antiquity ''1'' restored on Quispiguanca', '70bd951269555bbae218b13b7fe9c70e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86466", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2143:chunk-0001: description ''(1464-1525 AD) Quispiguanca was a royal estate of Inca emperor Huayna Capac. The ruins are located in the northern part of the present-day town of Urubamba, Peru, at an elevation of 2,910 metres (9,550 ft). This site served as an elegant country palace and, at times, a fortress to protect against rivals for power. The estate exemplifies the practice of Inca emperors acquiring large royal properties to increase their wealth and authority, which could then be inherited by their descendants.'' -> ''Quispiguanca was a royal estate of the Inca emperor Huayna Capac (c. 1464–1525 CE) [1]. The ruins of the estate are located in the northern part of the present-day town of Urubamba, Peru at an elevation of 2,910 metres [1]. The estate of Huayna Capac extended for 15 kilometres up and down the Sacred Valley [1]. The archaeological remains consist of a terrace, a well—preserved wall, gatehouses on the east side of the site, and several structures in poor condition in the northern third of the site [1]. Most of the construction is of fitted stonework, although some adobe and plaster were also used [1]. The original palace compound was rectangular and measured within its walls 189 metres north-south and 125 metres east-west [1]. The northernmost part of the compound consists of agricultural terraces and the stone foundation of a great hall, measuring 14 metres by 44 metres [1]. The Spanish conquistador of the Inca Empire, Francisco Pizarro, appropriated the estate of Huayna Capac as his encomienda in the 1530s [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121649", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: lat ''-13.180291063036304'' -> ''-13.301367''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121650", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: lon ''-72.0644785466515'' -> ''-72.112173''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121651", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''1000 - 1500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121652", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251535", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_name None -> ''1000 - 1500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251536", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_start None -> ''1000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386629", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''1000 - 1500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386630", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''1000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
