. It was inhabited during the Neolithic and Early Helladic periods, and used as a cemetery between the Late Helladic II period and Late Helladic IIIB (that is, c.\\u20091450 – c.\\u20091180 BCE) [1]. The cemetery consists of a tholos tomb, three tumuli and sixteen chamber tombs, and is one of the richest known from the Mycenaean period [1]. Persson named the tholos tomb the \"Royal Tomb\", and determined that it dated to the Late Helladic IIIA period (c.\\u20091350 BCE) [1]. The cemetery at Dendra was first excavated in 1926, when Nikolaos Bertos, the local ephor of the Greek Archaeological Service, invited Persson to excavate its tholos tomb [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105148", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105149", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158266", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a68e0f4e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a68e0f4e/Dendra 2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251571", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251572", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314988", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-010: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a68e0f4e/Dendra 2.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a68e0f4e/Dendra_tholos_tomb.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351768", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351769", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-