 fortress became the Roman colony of Puteoli in 194 BCE and was subsequently reinforced by Roman walls [1]. An ancient Roman temple dating from this time was reconstructed as a temple for Augustus in the 1st century CE in the centre of the fortress [1]. The temple was later converted into the Pozzuoli Cathedral which stands to this day [1]. Rione Terra was populated until 1970 when it was evacuated due to a sudden bradyseism event that raised the hill on which the district is located by 1.7 m relative to sea level [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158441", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2e/Rione_Terra_visto_dal_porto_di_Pozzuoli_%282010%29_by_RaBoe-22.jpg'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/ab336181/L''antico decumano sepolto.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:315673", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-011: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/ab336181/L''antico decumano sepolto.webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/ab336181/Rione_Terra_visto_dal_porto_di_Pozzuoli_(2010)_by_RaBoe-22.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('aba085f1-0a92-44a7-904a-5aac35c0aa40'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:aba085f1-0a92-44a7-904a-5aac35c0aa40:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''5'' restored on Quanterness Chambered Cairn', 'fc7aafde090e588c318ff42500a6edb5', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Cairn'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 20 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81182", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2023:chunk-0001: description ''Quanterness Chambered Cairn is a Neolithic burial monument on Mainland, Orkney, Scotland[1]. Excavations in the 1970s revealed an Iron Age roundhouse built into the cairn around 700 BC[1]. The burial chamber contained remains of at least 157 individuals alongside pottery and artefacts[1]. The site was designated a scheduled monument by Historic Environment Scotland in 1929[1]. It stands at the base of Wideford Hill.'' -> ''Quanterness chambered cairn is a Neolithic burial monument located on Mainland, Orkney in Scotland [1]. An Iron Age roundhouse built into the cairn was discovered during excavation in the early 1970s [1]. The dwelling was constructed around 700 BC [1]. Also found during excavation, were the remains of 157 people, pottery remnants and other artefacts [1]. The cairn is now a large grass-covered mound, 30 m in diameter and 3.2 m in height [1]. A long entrance passage led from the east end of the cairn into a long chamber, 6.5m by 1.9 m and 3.5 m high [1]. The cairn is a Maeshowe type of chambered cairn [1]. Radiocarbon dating has placed its construction to around 3400 BC [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158450", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Chambered_Cairn_and_Farm_House_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1075905.jpg/400px-Chambered_Cairn_and_Farm_House_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1075905.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/aba085f1/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
