 in particular a rectangular area 14.5 by 32 metres just inside the eastern entrance, thought to be a Roman granary [1]. Aerial photographs of 1965 and 1976 showed that the original Iron Age fort probably occupied most of the hilltop; this suggested that the visible defences date from the Roman period and that a Roman fort was built on a captured British fort [1]. The features seen were investigated by excavation in the early 1980s by Sheppard Frere and J. K. St Joseph [1]. The presence of the granary was confirmed [1]. Immediately to the west were three widely separated canabae, two-roomed huts thought to be accommodation for officers [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105983", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105984", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251965", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s015: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251966", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s015: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386657", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386658", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('ae28d423-c02b-44be-b78d-7d65c99f3c3b'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:ae28d423-c02b-44be-b78d-7d65c99f3c3b:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: antiquity ''7'' restored on Oakley Down Barrow Cemetery', '234f7a207875c33091db3b0de2f21871', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81184", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2023:chunk-0001: description ''Oakley Down Barrow Cemetery is one of the finest groups of Bronze Age round barrows on Cranborne Chase, located near Sixpenny Handley in Dorset, England. The scheduled monument comprises approximately 30 barrows of varied types including bowl, bell, and rare disc barrows, with most dating to 1400-1200 BC. Excavations revealed primary and secondary inhumations and cremations in urns, with grave goods including amber, glass and faience beads, and bronze daggers suggesting social differentiation. The site survived agricultural destruction through its protection as a royal hunting ground.'' -> \"Oakley Down Barrow Cemetery is a group of Bronze Age round barrows on Cranborne Chase, about 1 mile east of the village of Sixpenny Handley in Dorset, England [1]. The presence of Wor Barrow, a Neolithic long barrow nearby to the west, may have been influential in the construction of the Oakley Down cemetery [1]. There are about 30 barrows [1]. Many of the barrows were excavated in the early 19th century by Sir Richard Colt Hoare and William Cunnington; the barrows investigated can be identified from Hoare''s numbered plan [1]. The barrows contained primary and secondary inhumations, and primary and secondary cremations in urns and cists [1]. Grave goods included beads of amber, glass and faience, and bronze daggers [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105988", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:159089", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-024: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/96/Oakley_disc_barrow_panorama.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ae28d423/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251967", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s015: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251968", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s015: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345717", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345718", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386659", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386660", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-2500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
