nce on the west side, protected by an external bank 15 metres wide and 1 metre high, with traces of an external ditch [1]. This bank, branching out from the north west part of the rampart, runs south-west and then curves towards the fort, so that there is a passage into the fort from the south, at one point down to about 2 metres wide [1]. There are no traces of remains in the interior [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106085", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106086", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252351", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252352", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386685", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386686", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
