l slopes to the west and east, but is steepened to the north and south [1]. Near the centre of the enclosure is a small circular mound, diameter 10 metres and height 0.2 metres, on which is a modern trig point; the mound may possibly be a bowl barrow [1]. There has been partial excavation: objects found include Iron Age pottery sherds, hammer stones, flint flakes, scrapers and fragments of quern-stone [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122938", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:122940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s008: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:159302", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-024: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c4/Lynch_Farm_-_geograph.org.uk_-_528113.jpg'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252355", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252356", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386687", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386688", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
