ng La Trinité-sur-Mer [1]. The standing stones are made of weathered granite from local outcroppings that once extensively covered the area [1]. Three exceptionally large burial mounds are known from the Carnac and Morbihan area, dating from the mid-5th millennium BC and known collectively as ''Carnacéen tumuli'': Saint-Michel, Tumiac and Mané-er-Hroëk [1]. Each of these tumuli contained a megalithic burial chamber, containing the burial of only one individual, along with numerous large polished stone axeheads, stone arm-rings, and jewellery made from callaïs [1]. Scientific analyses have shown that many of the axeheads are made of jade from the Italian Alps, whilst the callaïs was imported from south-western Iberia [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:159969", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-025: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/b539ba9e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/b539ba9e/Mégalithes_vus_depuis_la_Maison_des_Mégalithes_à_Carnac_le_1er_septembre_2019_-_2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:315858", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/b539ba9e/Mégalithes_vus_depuis_la_Maison_des_Mégalithes_à_Carnac_le_1er_septembre_2019_-_2.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/b539ba9e/Carnac_megalith_alignment_1.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('b587a652-f222-47e6-adc9-b6ba1fa62722'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:b587a652-f222-47e6-adc9-b6ba1fa62722:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Frankenbury Camp', 'a43beeb0fd5c138f805d11bdd0939aa1', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(50.93645547766827, -1.7632570874696778, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86952", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2157:chunk-0001: description \"Frankenbury Camp is an Iron Age univallate hillfort on the northwestern edge of the New Forest in Hampshire, and the largest Iron Age hillfort in the New Forest area. The fort encloses approximately 4.4 hectares (11 acres) on a slight promontory overlooking the Avon Valley, with very steep natural slopes defending the west and south sides, while the northeast is protected by a rampart and ditch. Classified by Historic England as a ''slight univallate hillfort'' dating from c. 700 BC to AD 43, such sites are relatively rare nationally with only around 150 examples recorded. It is a scheduled ancient monument (no. 122).\" -> ''Frankenbury Camp is the site of an Iron Age univallate hillfort located in Hampshire [1]. The site is on a very slight promontory overlooking the Avon Valley on the north-western edge of the New Forest [1]. The fort encloses approximately 11 acres [1]. It has very steep natural slopes on the west and south sides [1]. The northeast sides are defended by a simple rampart and ditch [1]. The original entrance on the southeast corner has since been widened [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106806", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106807", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106808", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252385", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252386", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387295", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387296", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
