    ('b777562e-098d-4091-988f-79fe2b58db6c'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:b777562e-098d-4091-988f-79fe2b58db6c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''6'' restored on Snowden Crags', '245e80a16d945660e0f583b88bb7912f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Stone circle'', ''Undated'') is shared by 40 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86998", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2158:chunk-0001: description ''Snowden Crags is a stone circle on Askwith Moor in North Yorkshire, England [1]. Local antiquarian Eric Cowling first documented the site, which includes a stone circle and concentration of cairns, in his 1946 survey [1]. The monument remained largely hidden beneath dense heather for most of the year, keeping it obscure for decades [1]. Amateur archaeologist Paul Bennett rediscovered the site in 2010 and provided a detailed description of the stone circle, additionally noting a robber trench of unknown date at its centre [1].'' -> ''Snowden Crags is a prehistoric archaeological site on Askwith Moor in North Yorkshire [1]. Local antiquarian Eric Cowling recorded a stone circle and a concentration of cairns at the location in a 1946 survey, but the site remained obscure due to the density of heather covering it for most of the year [1]. It was rediscovered in 2010 by amateur archaeologist Paul Bennett, who described the stone circle in more detail and noted the presence of a robber trench of unknown date at its centre [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_lo