rge portal stones outside the circumference of the circle [1]. Such portal openings can also be found at Long Meg and Her Daughters, 64 km to the northeast in the Eden Valley [1]. In 1901, the Cumberland & Westmorland Antiquarian & Archaeological Society sponsored the first archaeological excavation at Swinside [1]. The excavators reported finding a lump of charcoal and a piece of decayed bone as well as some modern coins in the turf layer [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107895", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107896", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160831", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8c/Swinside_Stone_Circle_02.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c097eec0/Swinside Stone Circle 01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252833", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252834", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316650", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c097eec0/Swinside Stone Circle 01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c097eec0/Swinside_Stone_Circle_02.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357319", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357320", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2900''"}]'::jsonb),
