    ('c10a35c7-ca6a-49ad-b620-7467aaca6b61'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:c10a35c7-ca6a-49ad-b620-7467aaca6b61:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Caer Euni', '8dba53481cb6c3c7da49fb8a311c0a7a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(52.95989666733142, -3.4891559738550524, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87242", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2165:chunk-0001: description ''Caer Euni is an Iron Age hillfort in Gwynedd, Wales, situated on a narrow ridge about 4 km north-east of Llandderfel and 8 km north-east of Bala Lake [1]. The elongated enclosure measures roughly 216 m by 58 m, oriented north-east to south-west along the ridge. A rampart encloses the inner area, with a steep unbroken slope on the south-eastern side providing natural defence [2]. The fort shows evidence of enlargement during its occupation, and vitrified stone has been identified in the south-western rampart, indicating possible ancient burning [2]. The site offers panoramic views across the surrounding landscape [2].'' -> ''Caer Euni is an Iron Age hillfort, about 2.5 miles north-east of the village of Llandderfel and about 5 miles north-east of Llyn Tegid, in Gwynedd [1]. The fort is situated on a narrow ridge, at height 365 metres [1]. It is an elongated enclosure, length about 216 metres and width 58 metres, orientated north-east to south-west, aligned with the ridge [1]. There is a rampart enclosing the inner area, with a steep slope to the south-east and ditches and counterscarps elsewhere [1]. The principal entrance is in the north-east [1]. The fort was enlarged: there is a bank, formerly the south-west end, traceable across the interior, and further defences were built to the south-west, notably a large rock-cut ditch and a rampart built with the stone from the ditch [1]. The sites of about 25 round huts, diameter 15–20 feet, have been detected, mostly in the later part of the enclosure [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107904", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107905", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252837", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252838", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387342", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387343", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
