ed in The Wiltshire Archaeological and Natural History Magazine, while detailing it in greater depth in his unpublished notebooks [1]. He recorded the circle as consisting of eight stones at that time, with a possible avenue or stone row emerging from it and facing in the direction of the circle at Coate [1]. Later archaeologists have noted that some of the sarsens used as building material in Hodson were once part of the circle [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107941", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252863", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252864", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352742", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352743", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
