 and the sides were walled with flint [1]. Finds included a shield boss and fragments of an urn or drinking cup [1]. Among other finds were human bones and flint scrapers [1]. Further excavation was carried out in 1996 and 1997 [1]. The report on this work describes the periodic occupation of the hillfort between the 6th and 2nd centuries BC and suggests that it was a communal centre for various activities, including sheep management and exchange [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107961", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107962", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-500'' -> ''-600''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161430", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6e/Segsbury_Camp_aerial_image_sunset.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c40df04b/Segsbury_Camp_ditch.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324639", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c40df04b/Segsbury_Camp_ditch.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c40df04b/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:326011", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c40df04b/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c40df04b/Segsbury Camp aerial image sunset.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
