    ('c5851dba-f3f4-4aaf-a4a1-37bf6a56600b'::uuid, 'antiquity', '5', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:c5851dba-f3f4-4aaf-a4a1-37bf6a56600b:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: antiquity ''7'' restored on Micheldever Wood', '3dba6a27006b0f4b4c6eeb6f9768d5ce', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 5 from period_start None"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87322", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2168:chunk-0001: description ''Micheldever Wood is a Bronze Age to Romano-British archaeological site in Hampshire, England, located about 8 km (5 mi) north-east of Winchester near the village of Micheldever [1]. The woodland preserves prehistoric earthworks and settlement remains dating from the Bronze Age (c. 3000–1500 BC) through to the Romano-British period [1][2]. Notable features include Bronze Age burial mounds and field systems, as well as the ruins of a Roman villa [1]. The site is managed by Forestry England and is a scheduled monument, protected for its archaeological importance [1].'' -> ''Micheldever Wood is a wood near the village of Micheldever, in Hampshire, England, about 5 miles north-east of Winchester [1]. Archaeological features survive from the Bronze Age to the Romano-British period, preserved for many centuries by the woodland [1]. Information boards are provided for some of the features [1]. There is a Bronze Age cross dyke in the south-east of the wood, extending into Itchen Wood to the south; it is thought to mark a territorial boundary [1]. It is a bank 3 metres wide, with a ditch either side; th