rritorial boundary [1]. It is a bank 3 metres wide, with a ditch either side; the part of the dyke in Micheldever Wood is about 90 metres long [1]. There is a linear earthwork running west–east across the wood [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124169", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124170", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253187", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253188", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:326012", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c5851dba/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c5851dba/Micheldever Woods Bowl Barrow.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352761", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352762", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387360", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387361", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-2500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('c59b8485-583b-4c64-8d5b-61e046ed3437'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:c59b8485-583b-4c64-8d5b-61e046ed3437:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''5'' restored on Cairnpapple Hill', 'e4b8f7624b573afbef4bb35909d5adc4', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Cairn'', ''4500 - 3000 BC'') is shared by 20 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37495", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0057:chunk-0001: description \"Cairnpapple Hill is one of mainland Scotland''s most important prehistoric sites, used as a ritual center for over 4,000 years from the 4th millennium BC to the early Christian era. The earliest traces are six hearths dating from c. 3500 BC, containing pottery and stone-axe fragments from Wales and Cumbria. These were succeeded by a Neolithic henge monument featuring a bank 60m across with a ring of 24 timber posts. During the Bronze Age the site transitioned to funerary use, with cist burials accompanied by Beaker pottery and a wooden face mask, later covered by successive cairns. Excavated by Professor Piggott in 1947-48.\" -> ''Cairnpapple Hill is a hill with a dominating position in central lowland Scotland with views from coast to coast [1]. It was used and re-used as a major ritual site for around 4,000 years [1]. In the 19th century the site was completely concealed by trees, then in 1947–1948 excavations by Stuart Piggott found a series of ritual monuments from successive prehistoric periods [1]. Neolithic rituals began around 3500 BC with signs of small hearths, and precious objects left on the hill, presumably as offerings [1]. Probably around 3000 BC a Class II henge was constructed with the hilltop being surrounded by a bank outside a ditch about 12 ft wide cut over 3 ft into the rock [1]. Some time later a Bronze Age ritual added a small stone and clay cairn just off-centre inside the monument [1]. Under the cairn traces were found of at least one burial, with wooden objects (perhaps a mask and club) and beaker people style pottery which indicates a date around 2000 BC [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161479", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c59b8485/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c59b8485/Cairnpapple Hill alt1.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
