mbs and the ruins of a prehistoric settlement, possibly identified with that of ancient Mesatis [1]. Most of the explored graves were carved in circular, square, horseshoe or quadrilateral form with a dome, of varying dimensions often housing multiple burials [1]. All of the tombs revealed objects of everyday life, such as vases, jewellery, tools, weapons and utensils [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108005", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108006", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161481", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/%CE%92%CE%9F%CE%A5%CE%9D%CE%A4%CE%95%CE%9D%CE%97_09.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c5a5ae3a/Tomb75_interior.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316762", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c5a5ae3a/Tomb75_interior.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c5a5ae3a/ΒΟΥΝΤΕΝΗ_09.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('c5d05e95-f6a3-454f-85ba-6ebb4736b7bb'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:c5d05e95-f6a3-454f-85ba-6ebb4736b7bb:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''6'' restored on Arch of Augustus', '4fc74766cf909dfc044747f7b42c8d1f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Gate/archway/bridge'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 26 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37497", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0057:chunk-0001: description ''The Arch of Augustus (Arco di Augusto) is a Roman triumphal arch built in 27 BC in Rimini, Emilia-Romagna, Italy [1]. The arch is one of the oldest surviving Roman arches [1].'' -> ''The Arch of Augustus is a monument in the city of Aosta, northern Italy [1]. It was erected in 25 BC on the occasion of the Roman victory over the Salassi and was the work of Aulus Terentius Varro Murena [1]. It is located at the end of the decumanus maximus [1]. Constructed from conglomerate, the arch has a single vault, with a height to the keystone of 11.4 metres [1]. Its span is a barrel vault, constituting an extension in width of a round arch [1]. In the monument, various styles can be recognised: The ten engaged columns which decorate its facade and its sides culminate in Corinthian capitals, while the entablature, adorned with metopes and triglyphs, is of the Doric order [1]. During the 12th century, the arch contained the home of a local noble family and in 1318 a small fortification was built inside it, designed for a corps of crossbowmen [1]. In 1716, because of the numerous leaks that were compromising the integrity of the monument, the attic that previously crowned the arch was replaced with a slate roof [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:342329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "insert-2026-10-07-007-001: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/c5d05e95/Arco di augusto di sera.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
