reted as representing a sorcerer [1]. It is a representation of a human figure, whose head, in a trapezoidal configuration, ends in points resembling a pair of branches [1]. The remaining sculptures can be found either on the interior walls of the cave or on the floor [1]. The iconographic diversity is great with dimples, perpendicular features, semicircles and straight and interconnected bars, almost labyrinthine [1]. There is also an element in the form of a snake and human figures, chronologically bounded between the end of the Neolithic period and the beginning of the Chalcolithic / Bronze Age [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124176", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124177", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:124178", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''Rock relief/carving'' -> ''Rock art''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161505", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Abrigo_rupestre_da_Solhapa_-_Freguesia_de_Duas_Igrejas,_concelho_de_Miranda_do_Douro,_distrito_de_Bragança,_Portugal_-_13.jpg/400px-Abrigo_rupestre_da_Solhapa_-_Freguesia_de_Duas_Igrejas,_concelho_de_Miranda_do_Douro,_distrito_de_Bragança,_Portugal_-_13.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c663e466/Abrigo rupestre da Solhapa - Freguesia de Duas Igrejas, concelho de Miranda do Douro, distrito de Bragança, Portugal - 15.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253197", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253198", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-100