    ('c8af8070-bdd2-46a4-b651-a87fadb09bfe'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:c8af8070-bdd2-46a4-b651-a87fadb09bfe:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Knoll Camp', '2d7787e2febe85d5ed5d56a2c8fa2395', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(50.96615537833616, -1.85993218931901, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87414", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2171:chunk-0001: description ''Knoll Camp (or Damerham Knoll) is an Iron Age univallate hillfort in Hampshire, England, on the border with Wiltshire near the village of Rockbourne. The circular earthwork encloses about 1.6 hectares (4 acres), defined by a single ditch with inner rampart reaching 1.2m above the ditch base. Dating to the Late Bronze Age to Early Iron Age transition (8th-5th centuries BC), it likely served as a stock enclosure or place of refuge. Associated features include a 132m cross dyke and a 705m linear earthwork. The site is a Scheduled Ancient Monument.'' -> ''Knoll Camp, or Damerham Knoll, is the site of an Iron Age univallate hill fort located in Hampshire [1]. The fort comprises a circular earthwork containing about four acres [1]. There is a single ditch with inner rampart and traces of counter scarp bank [1]. The site is a scheduled ancient monument no.118 [1]. The site is located at grid reference SU099185, to the west of the village of Rockbourne in the county of Hampshire [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108057", "url": "remediat