    ('dba6e82d-3388-4b6c-beba-63f8f440ba0b'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:dba6e82d-3388-4b6c-beba-63f8f440ba0b:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Brent Knoll Camp', '500f1c0b3b96ddb187269bd7ea49f9a6', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(51.2542606791643, -2.945491229779002, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81368", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2030:chunk-0001: description ''Brent Knoll Camp is an Iron Age hillfort crowning the 137 m Brent Knoll near Burnham-on-Sea, Somerset, a dramatic landmark rising above the flat Somerset Levels. Before drainage, the knoll was an island known as the Isle of Frogs. The fort encloses 1.6 hectares within multiple ramparts following the hill contours, with a wall around 10 m high and a ditch on the east side. Human settlement dates to at least the Bronze Age. The Romans later used the summit as a fortification, and an urn containing coins of emperors Trajan and Severus was found before 1790. Now a Scheduled Monument in National Trust care.'' -> ''Brent Knoll Camp is an Iron Age hillfort at Brent Knoll, 3 kilometres from Burnham-on-Sea, Somerset [1]. It has been designated as a Scheduled Monument [1]. Before the Somerset Levels were drained, Brent Knoll was an island, known as the Isle of Frogs, that provided a safe haven from the water and marshes [1]. The Romans used its summit as a fortification [1]. An urn containing coins of the Roman Emperors Trajan and Severus was found at the site before 1790 [1]. Other finds have included pennant sandstone roof tiles and painted wall plaster, indicative of a substantial building that is more likely to have been a temple than a villa [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109770", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109771", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254117", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254118", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318403", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dba6e82d/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dba6e82d/Brent Knoll hill fort - geograph.org.uk - 286891.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387422", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387423", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
