eople lived in the caves [1]. Thereafter, it was used for storage and worship [1]. The cave may have once been a shrine to a female deity - Artemis, Diktynna or perhaps Eileithyia [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254133", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254134", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353740", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353741", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387430", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387431", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-6500''"}]'::jsonb),
