both within the circle and around the cairn [1]. These remains were often though not always placed in ceramic urns, and were sometimes deposited alongside other material such as flint tools, small pieces of bronze, and faience beads [1]. The antiquarian Thomas Bateman excavated at the site in 1852, and J. P. Heathcote conducted a second excavation between 1931 and 1933 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110496", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110497", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164409", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/Doll_Tor_stone_circle,_Derbyshire.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243824", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243825", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:326247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/Doll_Tor_stone_circle,_Derbyshire.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dfe76079/Doll tor stone circle.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
