stonbury Castle [1]. Inside the fort, on the western side, is an 11th- or 12th-century motte with a surrounding narrow inner bailey [1]. The ramparts of the earlier hillfort may have been used as the outer bailey of the castle [1]. The first documentary reference to Hembury Castle is in the 13th-century cartulary of nearby Buckfast Abbey, where it is referred to as vetus castellum quod dicitur Hembire [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110509", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110510", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254153", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254154", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:326279", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e1037d75/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e1037d75/Hembury Castle 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387436", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387437", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
