 The sculpture is made of white marble and carved in very high relief [1]. It is now kept at the Kerameikos Archaeological Museum in Athens with inventory number P687 [1]. The relief bears the inscription \"Demetria and Pamphile\", the names of the two women depicted [1]. The naiskos shows two grown up women, one sitting on a luxurious chair, while the other stands still beside her [1]. The sitting woman is the recently deceased one, Pamphile, while the standing one is her sister Demetria, who had long predeceased her [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:125677", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s010: site_type ''Monument'' -> ''Funerary''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164516", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e2fc0a30/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e2fc0a30/IG II² 11088(1).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318534", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e2fc0a30/IG II² 11088(1).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e2fc0a30/The_Grave_Stele_of_Demetria_and_Pamphile_(4th_cent._B.C.)_at_the_Archaeological_Museum_of_Kerameikos_on_27_June_2018.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('e355bfda-5a11-4b50-813f-8212abdd0009'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:e355bfda-5a11-4b50-813f-8212abdd0009:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''5'' restored on Tischofer Cave', 'beda18bd21ec648860cf67b6391f5d91', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Cave Structures'', ''Undated'') is shared by 52 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81388", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2031:chunk-0001: description ''The Tischofer Cave is a cave in the Kaisertal valley in the Kaisergebirge mountains of Austria. The roughly 40 metre long cave, about 8.5 metres high at the entrance, was occupied by cave bears during the Paleolithic as evidenced by numerous excavated skeletal remains [1]. Bone tools made of cave bear bones and skulls, dated to about 27,000–28,000 years ago, were discovered here [1]. This makes the Tischofer Cave the oldest known uncontested site of human occupation in Tyrol [1]. The cave also served as a locally important gathering place and weapons cache during the Tyrolean Rebellion in the Napoleonic Wars [1].'' -> ''The Tischofer Cave is a cave in the Kaisertal valley in the Kaisergebirge mountains in Austria [1]. The roughly 40 m long cave, which is about 8.5 m high at the entrance, was occupied by cave bears and other predators as shelter during the Paleolithic as evidenced by numerous excavated skeletal remains [1]. Bone tools of paleo-human inhabitants made of cave bear bones and skulls discovered here and dated to about 27,000 - 28,000 years ago may be viewed in the local history museum in the fortress at Kufstein [1]. That dating makes the Tischofer Cave the oldest known uncontested site of human occupation in Tyrol [1]. Discoveries of more recent human skeletons and associated tools also indicate that the cave served as a copper smithy and foundry during the Bronze Age [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110557", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110558", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164526", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/WAF-Exkursion_Vorderkaiserfelden_16.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e355bfda/Tischoferhöhle I.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254181", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254182", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318543", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e355bfda/Tischoferhöhle I.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e355bfda/WAF-Exkursion_Vorderkaiserfelden_16.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353765", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353766", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
