 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387449", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('e4f6fa32-6aff-4539-b40b-ab73f9e94cec'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '6', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:e4f6fa32-6aff-4539-b40b-ab73f9e94cec:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: mystery ''6'' restored on Sammallahdenmäki', '816a245b24dc04786ad2dbb0127b5fc8', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Cemetery'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 7 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88114", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2191:chunk-0001: description ''Sammallahdenmäki is a Bronze Age burial site in Finland near Rauma, in Satakunta. The site comprises 33 granite burial cairns dating to 1500-500 BC, representing over 3,000 years of history[1]. It is one of the largest and most complete Bronze Age sites in Fennoscandia[1]. In 1999, Sammallahdenmäki was designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site[1].'' -> ''Sammallahdenmäki is a Bronze Age burial site in Finland in Rauma, in the region of Satakunta [1]. The burial site is located on a long ridge in a remote area off the road to Tampere from Rauma [1]. The 33 burial cairns making up the site are arranged into distinct clusters along the crest of the ridge [1]. Each cairn was constructed from granite boulders quarried from the cliff face below the ridge or collected on site, in typical Bronze Age fashion [1]. Two unusual cairns are the Huilun pitkä raunio (\"long ruin of Huilu\"), which is surrounded by an ancient stone wall, and the Kirkonlaattia (\"Church Floor\"), an unusual rectangular cairn covering 16 x 19 metres with a flat top [1]. Four of the cairns were excavated by archaeologist Volter Högman in 1891, including Huilun pitkä raunio and Kirkonlaattia [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110580", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110581", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165036", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cb/Sammallahdenm%C3%A4ki_Bronze_age_burial_site_Huilu_Long_ruin.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e4f6fa32/Sammallahdenmäki 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:335277", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e4f6fa32/Sammallahdenmäki 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e4f6fa32/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('e4f6fa32-6aff-4539-b40b-ab73f9e94cec'::uuid, 'rarity_score', '35', '32', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:e4f6fa32-6aff-4539-b40b-ab73f9e94cec:rarity_score', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: rarity_score ''32'' restored on Sammallahdenmäki', '816a245b24dc04786ad2dbb0127b5fc8', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "rarity_score = 35 from mystery 7, cultural_influence 7"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88114", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2191:chunk-0001: description ''Sammallahdenmäki is a Bronze Age burial site in Finland near Rauma, in Satakunta. The site comprises 33 granite burial cairns dating to 1500-500 BC, representing over 3,000 years of history[1]. It is one of the largest and most complete Bronze Age sites in Fennoscandia[1]. In 1999, Sammallahdenmäki was designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site[1].'' -> ''Sammallahdenmäki is a Bronze Age burial site in Finland in Rauma, in the region of Satakunta [1]. The burial site is located on a long ridge in a remote area off the road to Tampere from Rauma [1]. The 33 burial cairns making up the site are arranged into distinct clusters along the crest of the ridge [1]. Each cairn was constructed from granite boulders quarried from the cliff face below the ridge or collected on site, in typical Bronze Age fashion [1]. Two unusual cairns are the Huilun pitkä raunio (\"long ruin of Huilu\"), which is surrounded by an ancient stone wall, and the Kirkonlaattia (\"Church Floor\"), an unusual rectangular cairn covering 16 x 19 metres with a flat top [1]. Four of the cairns were excavated by archaeologist Volter Högman in 1891, including Huilun pitkä raunio and Kirkonlaattia [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110580", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110581", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165036", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cb/Sammallahdenm%C3%A4ki_Bronze_age_burial_site_Huilu_Long_ruin.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e4f6fa32/Sammallahdenmäki 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:335277", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e4f6fa32/Sammallahdenmäki 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e4f6fa32/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('e4f6fa32-6aff-4539-b40b-ab73f9e94cec'::uuid, 'total_power', '23', '22', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:e4f6fa32-6aff-4539-b40b-ab73f9e94cec:total_power', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: total_power ''22'' restored on Sammallahdenmäki', '816a245b24dc04786ad2dbb0127b5fc8', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "total_power = 23 from antiquity + fortification + cultural_influence + mystery + legacy = 6 + 2 + 7 + 7 + 1"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88114", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2191:chunk-0001: description ''Sammallahdenmäki is a Bronze Age burial site in Finland near Rauma, in Satakunta. The site comprises 33 granite burial cairns dating to 1500-500 BC, representing over 3,000 years of history[1]. It is one of the largest and most complete Bronze Age sites in Fennoscandia[1]. In 1999, Sammallahdenmäki was designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site[1].'' -> ''Sammallahdenmäki is a Bronze Age burial site in Finland in Rauma, in the region of Satakunta [1]. The burial site is located on a long ridge in a remote area off the road to Tampere from Rauma [1]. The 33 burial cairns making up the site are arranged into distinct clusters along the crest of the ridge [1]. Each cairn was constructed from granite boulders quarried from the cliff face below the ridge or collected on site, in typical Bronze Age fashion [1]. Two unusual cairns are the Huilun pitkä raunio (\"long ruin of Huilu\"), which is surrounded by an ancient stone wall, and the Kirkonlaattia (\"Church Floor\"), an unusual rectangular cairn covering 16 x 19 metres with a flat top [1]. Four of the cairns were excavated by archaeologist Volter Högman in 1891, including Huilun pitkä raunio and Kirkonlaattia [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110580", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110581", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165036", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cb/Sammallahdenm%C3%A4ki_Bronze_age_burial_site_Huilu_Long_ruin.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e4f6fa32/Sammallahdenmäki 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:335277", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e4f6fa32/Sammallahdenmäki 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e4f6fa32/hero.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('e500a4eb-0731-4902-8380-c5a19a9d2a2b'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:e500a4eb-0731-4902-8380-c5a19a9d2a2b:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Prideaux Castle', '85ba98503519d7fa91376ac7d6595709', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(50.36884522511713, -4.7305107316827035, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88116", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2191:chunk-0001: description \"Prideaux Castle is a multivallate Iron Age hillfort atop a 133m conical hill near Luxulyan in Cornwall. The quadrivallate defences consist of four concentric ramparts and ditches, with rampart heights ranging from 1.3m to 2.7m, enclosing approximately 0.81 hectares. Interior finds include flints, slingstones, a stone axe, and pottery sherds. As a small multivallate hillfort, it is regarded as a high-status permanent settlement. The site lies near the ancient tin trade route later known as the Saints'' Way, connecting it to Cornwall''s stannary economy.\" -> ''Prideaux Castle is a multivallate Iron Age hillfort situated atop a 133 m (435 ft) high conical hill near the southern boundary of the parish of Luxulyan, Cornwall, England [1]. It is also sometimes referred to as Prideaux Warren, Prideaux War-Ring, or Prideaux Hillfort [1]. The remains of the first and second circular ramparts are quite distinct, although overgrown with trees on the north and east sides [1]. They appear to be constructed of earth and rubble [1]. The third rampart is only fragmentarily represented, but easily traced, due to the vegetation [1]. A fourth, outermost wall is discerned on aerial photographs [1]. Without datable artifacts, the hillfort is nonetheless assigned to the Iron Age of pre-Roman Britain on the basis of its general form [1]. Because the enclosed area is less than 1 ha, it would be classified as a \"small multivallate hillfort\" [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110582", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110583", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165037", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/e500a4eb/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254199", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254200", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387450", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387451", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
