    ('e522ea1d-4166-429d-8cac-8d31f72b944b'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:e522ea1d-4166-429d-8cac-8d31f72b944b:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Mowsbury Hill', 'b90aacc2036af778e1f56af3603a7a9e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(52.16735258433723, -0.4421423757544208, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88118", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2191:chunk-0001: description ''Mowsbury Hill is a 2.8-hectare Scheduled Monument and Local Nature Reserve in north Bedford, England, containing one of only 10 univallate hillforts in Bedfordshire. Archaeological trenching in 1971-72 revealed a single ditch approximately 4.3m wide and 2m deep encircling the spur, with a timber-framework bank that had burnt down, leaving impressions in semi-fired clay; a human skull fragment was found in association with the destruction. The roughly oval plan measures 290m by 200m. In medieval times, it became a moated settlement identified with the Manor of Morinsbury, mentioned in documents before 1465.'' -> ''Mowsbury Hill is a 2.8 hectare Local Nature Reserve and Scheduled Monument in north Bedford [1]. Archaeological excavation has shown that the site is a univallate hillfort, and pottery dates to the early Iron Age, occupied for a limited period [1]. In medieval times it was a moated settlement with two fishponds in the Manor of Morinsbury [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110589", "url": "remediation_change_log", "qu