onnected dual citadels on Larisa and Aspis, and then continued around their eastern slopes to surround the classical city [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110647", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110648", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165139", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e7f9d07d/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e7f9d07d/Argos Castle 2021.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:244687", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:244688", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-1300''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319229", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e7f9d07d/Argos Castle 2021.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e7f9d07d/Argos3.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
