h-east of Keswick [1]. Carrock Fell is also the site of an Iron Age hill fort which crowns the summit [1]. Only the foundations of the walls remain [1]. The fort is oval shaped and is believed to have been built by the Celts and destroyed by the Romans in their conquest of northern England [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:125785", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:125786", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:125787", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s010: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:125788", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s010: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrock_Fell'' -> ''https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=7481''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165771", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-033: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ed3e4264/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254633", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254634", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319318", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url None -> ''/data/images/wiki/ed3e4264/Carrock_Fell_from_the_Caldew_Valley.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353833", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353834", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start '