    ('ee2d3797-494f-4588-98e8-23d6d76622c6'::uuid, 'empire_count', '1', '0', 'card-stats-2026-11-07-rollback:ee2d3797-494f-4588-98e8-23d6d76622c6:empire_count', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07: empire_count ''0'' restored on Kelsborrow Castle', '962af34757713edfa683d47ed470cc7c', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "empire_count = 1 from tag_site(53.20336141433445, -2.702054087332528, period_start None)"}, {"source": "production export d17040beec27c2c0 (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 900 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59700 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-05''s own export (2026-11-05 22:52:16.465314+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88330", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2197:chunk-0001: description ''Kelsborrow Castle is an Iron Age hill fort in Cheshire, one of only seven in the county. The fort was likely occupied for only a short period. Archaeological finds include a bronze palstave recovered in the 19th century. The site is protected as a Scheduled Ancient Monument. [1]'' -> ''Kelsborrow Castle is an Iron Age hill fort in Cheshire, northern England [1]. In the 19th century, a bronze palstave was recovered from the site [1]. Along with Eddisbury and Oakmere, Kelsborrow forms a small cluster of Iron Age hill forts within 3 miles of each other, near the Mouldsworth Gap [1]. As well as being a hill fort, Kelsborrow Castle is a type of promontory fort, as it exploits the natural steep slopes of the area to create a defensive site [1]. The site is surrounded by an artificial bank and ditch, although there is a gap in the ditch for around 400 ft in the west [1]. The best surviving parts of the bank are 6 ft high, and the distance between the outer edge of the ditch and the inner edge of the rampart is 100 ft [1]. The defences cover 1.75 acres, and enclose an area of 7.25 acres [1]. Geophysical surveys and small-scale archaeological excavations in 1973 and 1996 indicated that there may be structures such as storage pits buried within the hill fort [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111414", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:111415", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s022: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254641", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254642", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s021: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387470", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387471", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
