shire [1]. It is near the boundaries with Dorset and Wiltshire [1]. The site is a scheduled monument, and it is one of several archaeological features on Martin Down, such as Bokerley Dyke [1]. The enclosure is the original example of a type of prehistoric feature, the \"Martin Down style enclosure\": they are small enclosures of the Bronze Age, area often less than 0.3 hectares, considered to be domestic settlements [1]. The rectangular enclosure has internal dimensions of about 90 metres south-west to north-east by 63 metres [1]. It has a single bank of width up to 10 metres and up to 0.7 metres above the interior, and there is an external ditch [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112238", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112239", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112240", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Earthwork''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302214", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302215", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_start None -> ''-2000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387759", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s005: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387760", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s005: period_start ''-2000'' -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
