o respectively [1]. On the east slope is the Aglaureion, the largest of the Acropolis caves at 14m across the mouth [1]. Herodotus records that the Persians in 480 BCE used this part of the hill to scale the Acropolis [1]. Pausanias described the Aglaureion as being above the sanctuary of the Dioskouroi near the Prytaneion [1]. These sources were the only inconclusive clues to the location of the shrine which was not identified as its current site until the 1980 stele find [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112244", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112245", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:166640", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-034: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f7f6d178/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f7f6d178/The sanctuaries of Pan, Zeus, and Apollo on the Acropolis of Athens on March 22, 2021.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:255049", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s022: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:255050", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s022: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319979", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-016: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/f7f6d178/The sanctuaries of Pan, Zeus, and Apollo on the Acropolis of Athens on March 22, 2021.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f7f6d178/Zeus_and_Apollon_Ipakrion_caves_7233923.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354431", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s010: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354432", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fi