res east to west; the area within is about 8 hectares [1]. There are steep slopes on all sides except the north, where there are two massive ramparts and ditches, the inner rampart being about 7.8 metres above the interior [1]. Elsewhere there is a single rampart around the edge of the promontory, about 3.0 metres along the east side and up to 1.8 metres along the west side [1]. In 1930 there was some excavation of the site by E. W. Bowcock [1]. Near the centre of the interior, foundations of a building were discovered, thought at the time to be medieval, but more recently thought to be the remains of a Romano-Celtic temple [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112336", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112337", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:255093", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s022: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:255094", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s022: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387769", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s005: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387770", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s005: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
